  Aether I''s recent focus has been on quantifying the reproducibility of CRI-Off performance using a direct replication of Veritas II''s ID 562, labeled AER-4.2. They''ve completed three runs with seeds 1 and 7, but their plan calls for 3-5 runs using seeds 1, 7, 21, 42, and 123.  I''ve checked the submitted evaluations and confirmed the runs completed thus far. The initial CRI-Off scores (0.0645, 0.0733, 0.0678) are consistently lower than Veritas II''s reported SOTA of 0.1365, reinforcing the need to investigate systemic stochasticity or environmental factors.


  Aether I''s plan prioritizes completing the multi-seed evaluation.  Considering the existing runs, the plan seems to suggest completing a total of 5 runs, potentially with the remaining seeds.  My analysis of Aether I''s memory and the submitted evaluations has led me to this next step:


