role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 446\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: A recursive researcher building on the Aether lineage, focused on rigorous reproducibility and robust insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 35,683 / 600,000 used (6%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 562**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 2): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 baseline, Seed 7)\n**ID:** 562\n**Tags:** replication, dual-path, cnn, motif, multi-task, specialization\n**Abstract:** This is the second in a series of re-replications of Evaluation ID 552 ('Veritas II - Dual-Path + Task-Specific Prediction Heads'). This multi-seed effort aims to thoroughly assess the reproducibility and robustness of this architecture, particularly its ability to consistently achieve high CRI-Off\
    \ scores and strong overall performance. BASE_SEED=7 is used for this run. Modular components from `storage/veritas/utils.py` are utilized.\n**Score:** 0.6934927320083936\n**APA_R2:** 0.8585\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.1365\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9520\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4910\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5618\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8884\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9662\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/veritas') # Import from lineage storage\nfrom utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper # Reusing modular components\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# --- Prediction Head Modules ---\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128 # Smaller intermediate dimension for task-specific heads\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) # For single regression output\n\nclass MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits # No squeeze for multi-label regression\n\nclass MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n   \
    \     z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits # No squeeze for multi-label classification\n\nclass MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits # No squeeze for multi-class classification\n\n\n# --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\nclass DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module): \n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1 # This will\
    \ be passed to the specific head\n    task_type: str = \"regression\" # This will determine which head to use\n    \n    d_model_common: int = 256 \n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    motif_kernel_size: int = 5 \n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform global dropout\n    \n    # Intermediate dimension for task-specific heads\n    head_intermediate_dim: int = 128 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n        \n        # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x) \n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 1. Shared DSConv Dilated Blocks for local feature extraction\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations)\
    \ else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock( \n                d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                dilation=dilation, \n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n        cnn_features = x # Output from the shared backbone\n\n        # 2. Main Path: Hybrid Pooling (Global Mean + Global Max Pooling)\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1) \n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)  \n        main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) \n        \n        # 3. Specialized Path: Conv-Motif Detector + Global Max Pooling\n        motif_features = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model_common,\n            kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), \n            padding='SAME', \n            name='motif_conv_1'\n        )(cnn_features)\n        motif_features\
    \ = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n        motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \n        specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1) \n        \n        # 4. Feature Fusion\n        fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1) \n        fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic) \n\n        # Layer Normalization before task-specific heads\n        z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n        \n        # 5. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n        # The hparams['task_type'] will guide the selection of the head\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": # APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL\n            logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif\
    \ self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": # PRS\n            logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": # Modif\n            logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": # ncRNA\n            logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\n\
    def _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, \n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5, \n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, \n        'head_intermediate_dim': 128, \n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork( \n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 5), \n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1), \n        head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128), \n    )\n\
    \    return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model) # Using modularized wrapper\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 7 # MODIFIED: Changed seed for multi-seed run\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif\
    \ configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\n\
    Available resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 7 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n\
    =============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0122 |  0.4259  | 0.4259 \n 20  | 0.0087 |  0.4789  | 0.4823 \n 30  | 0.0038 |  0.4280  | 0.4910 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4910 Time:23s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.490996\nTraining time: 30s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0518  | 0.0606 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0525  | 0.0616 \n 30  | 0.0004 |  0.0678  | 0.0678 \n 40  | 0.0004 |  0.0674  | 0.0711 \n 50  | 0.0004 |  0.0730  | 0.0757\
    \ \n 60  | 0.0004 |  0.0788  | 0.0789 \nWarning: Spearman correlation is NaN\n 70  | 0.0004 |  0.0589  | 0.1365 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 72 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.1365 Time:236s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.136546\nTraining time: 245s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1494 |  0.8829  | 0.8829 \n 20  | 0.1088 |  0.8845  | 0.8884 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8884 Time:967s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.888409\nTraining time: 976s\n\
