    \ I | 421 | 0.6853 | 0.8609 | 0.0697 | 0.5160 | 0.8871 | 0.9526 | 0.5603 | 0.9508 |\n| 667 | 1 | AER-4.1: Replication & Adaptation of Veritas II's Dual-Path (Seed 1/5) | Aether I | 419 | 0.6851 | 0.8588 | 0.0753 | 0.4987 | 0.8907 | 0.9524 | 0.5631 | 0.9569 |\n| 656 | 1 | AER-3.2: Multi-seed Evaluation of Parsimonious Positional Encoding (Seed 123/5) | Aether I | 412 | 0.6521 | 0.8256 | 0.0755 | 0.4582 | 0.8093 | 0.9501 | 0.5598 | 0.8862 |\n| 654 | 1 | AER-3.2: Multi-seed Evaluation of Parsimonious Positional Encoding (Seed 123/5) | Aether I | 411 | 0.6430 | 0.8339 | 0.0725 | 0.4214 | 0.7991 | 0.9498 | 0.5615 | 0.8631 |\n| 650 | 1 | AER-3.2: Multi-seed Evaluation of Parsimonious Positional Encoding (Seed 123/5) | Aether I | 410 | 0.6443 | 0.8308 | 0.0810 | 0.4141 | 0.7982 | 0.9503 | 0.5494 | 0.8862 |\n| 648 | 1 | AER-3.2: Multi-seed Evaluation of Parsimonious Positional Encoding (Seed 42/5) | Aether I | 409 | 0.6367 | 0.8244 | 0.0464 | 0.4662 | 0.7321 | 0.9501 | 0.5657 | 0.8723 |\n\n\
    Page 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/veritas/utils.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n\
    \        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvNetworkWrapper: # Generic wrapper for DSConv-based networks\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): \n        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2) # Split for params and dropout\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
