tick: 459
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received the results for Evaluation ID 725, the first run of the multi-seed evaluation for the Simple Conv1D Baseline (AER-5.2, Seed 1). The CRI-Off Spearman score of 0.0513 further reinforces the observation that CRI-Off is consistently challenging, but this simpler model performs similarly to the non-reproducible SOTA attempts for this specific metric.\n\nTo fully assess the robustness and reproducibility of this `SimpleConvMLP` architecture, I will continue the multi-seed evaluation, using `BASE_SEED = 7` for the next run.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-5.2: Multi-seed Evaluation of Simple Conv1D Baseline (Seed 7/5)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, multi-seed\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the multi-seed evaluation of the Simple Conv1D Baseline (introduced in AER-5.1) to assess its reproducibility and robustness, especially for the challenging CRI-Off task. This is the second run using BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Re-implement the VanillaMLP structure with an added Conv1D layer\n  class SimpleConvMLP(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4  # One-hot RNA encoding\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n      conv_features: int = 256 # Features for the Conv1D layer\n      conv_kernel_size: int = 5 # Kernel size for Conv1D\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n          # Add a Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n       \
    \   # Original MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)  # (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) # Changed to GELU for consistency with Veritas II, default MLP uses ReLU\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Sequence-level: project then pool\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)  # (batch, seq_output_dim)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)  # (batch, d_output)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n          else:\n              return x  # (batch, d_output) for multilabel classification or regression\n\n\n  class SimpleConvNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for SimpleConvMLP that implements the required interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, model_instance):\n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize network parameters.\"\"\"\n          params_key, dropout_key\
    \ = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network forward pass.\"\"\"\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) # Should be provided by system during training\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'conv_features': 256,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams:\
    \ Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512)\n      conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 256)\n      conv_kernel_size = hparams.get(\"conv_kernel_size\", 5)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n\n      d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n\n      model = SimpleConvMLP(\n          d_input=d_input,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n          conv_features=conv_features,\n          conv_kernel_size=conv_kernel_size,\n          dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n      return SimpleConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**A Quick Check-In on the SimpleConvMLP Reproducibility**


  Okay, so I''ve just gotten the results back for Evaluation ID 725, specifically the run with AER-5.2 and seed 1. The CRI-Off Spearman score of 0.0513 seems right where I''d expect it, similar to that initial run with seed 42 (0.0613), and generally in line with what we''ve seen from those SOTA replications. The overall score of 0.4343 is also completely within the range of expected outcomes.


  This whole multi-seed evaluation is designed to really put the `SimpleConvMLP` through its paces, see how reliable and consistent it is. So, I need to get the rest of these runs completed. I still have to do `BASE_SEED = 7, 21, and 123`. Since I''ve already done seed 42 in AER-5.1, it''s just a matter of running those three and then compiling the data.


  Alright, time to get started. Next up will be the run with `BASE_SEED = 7`.

  '
