tick: 461
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received the results for Evaluation ID 728 (AER-5.2, Seed 7). The CRI-Off Spearman score of 0.0611, along with the previous run's 0.0513, shows a consistent performance for CRI-Off within a narrow range, which is a positive indication of robustness compared to the observed irreproducibility of the higher SOTA score.\n\nTo further establish the reproducibility of this `SimpleConvMLP` architecture, I will continue the multi-seed evaluation. The next seed in the sequence is 21.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-5.2: Multi-seed Evaluation of Simple Conv1D Baseline (Seed 21/5)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, multi-seed\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the multi-seed evaluation of the Simple Conv1D Baseline (introduced in AER-5.1) to assess its reproducibility and robustness, especially for the challenging CRI-Off task. This is the third run using BASE_SEED=21.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax\
    \ import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Re-implement the VanillaMLP structure with an added Conv1D layer\n  class SimpleConvMLP(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4  # One-hot RNA encoding\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n      conv_features: int = 256 # Features for the Conv1D layer\n      conv_kernel_size: int = 5 # Kernel size for Conv1D\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n          # Add a Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Original MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)\
    \  # (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) # Changed to GELU for consistency with Veritas II, default MLP uses ReLU\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Sequence-level: project then pool\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)  # (batch, seq_output_dim)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)  # (batch, d_output)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n          else:\n              return x  # (batch, d_output) for multilabel classification or regression\n\n\n  class SimpleConvNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for SimpleConvMLP that implements the required interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, model_instance):\n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \"\"\"Initialize network parameters.\"\"\"\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network forward pass.\"\"\"\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) # Should be provided by system during training\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'conv_features': 256,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\"\
    , 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512)\n      conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 256)\n      conv_kernel_size = hparams.get(\"conv_kernel_size\", 5)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n\n      d_input = 4 # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n\n      model = SimpleConvMLP(\n          d_input=d_input,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n          conv_features=conv_features,\n          conv_kernel_size=conv_kernel_size,\n          dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n      return SimpleConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n\
    \  BASE_SEED = 21\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Assessing the Simple Conv1D Baseline**


  Okay, I''ve got the results back for Evaluation ID 728 – the second run using multiple seeds for that Simple Conv1D Baseline, specifically with AER-5.2 and Seed 7. The CRI-Off Spearman score is 0.0611, which falls right in line with what we''ve been seeing with the SOTA replication attempts and, importantly, surpasses that Vanilla MLP baseline.


  This consistency, seeing similar results across Seeds 1 and 7, is really a good sign for the `SimpleConvMLP` in terms of the CRI-Off metric. It''s more stable than that single top score we saw with Veritas II. I''m after a *reliable* architecture for this CRI-Off thing, not just a one-off high score if we can''t reproduce it.


  So, I''ll keep this multi-seed evaluation going. The next seed in the common sequence is 21.


  I just need to remember to submit the exact same code, but with `BASE_SEED = 21` this time.

  '
