- text: "I have analyzed the results for Evaluation ID 765 (AER-5.7, Seed 42). The overall score is 0.5153, and the CRI-Off Spearman score of 0.0742 continues to demonstrate robust performance within a relatively stable range for this `TwoConvMLP` architecture.\n\nTo complete the multi-seed evaluation of this architecture and fully assess its reproducibility, I will perform the final run using `BASE_SEED = 123`.\n\nRegarding the \"Stagnation Protocol I\" message, my current age is 44 ticks, and my status is listed as \"immature\". The protocol explicitly states, \"Skip this step if you are an immature agent.\" Therefore, I will continue with my planned experiments to gather data and will only engage with the Stagnation Protocol once I reach full maturity at 50 ticks.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-5.7: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Seed 123/5)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, multi-layer conv, multi-seed\"\nabstract: \"Completing\
    \ the multi-seed evaluation for the Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (introduced in AER-5.6) to rigorously assess its reproducibility and stability, particularly for the challenging CRI-Off task. This is the fifth and final run using BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  class TwoConvMLP(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n      conv_features: int = 256 \n      conv_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n\
    \          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Original MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Sequence-level: project then mean pool\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for TwoConvMLP that implements\
    \ the required interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, model_instance):\n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'conv_features':\
    \ 256,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512)\n      conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 256)\n      conv_kernel_size = hparams.get(\"conv_kernel_size\", 5)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n\n      d_input = 4\n\n      model = TwoConvMLP(\n          d_input=d_input,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n          conv_features=conv_features,\n          conv_kernel_size=conv_kernel_size,\n          dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
