tick: 482
role: model
parts:
- text: "I apologize for attempting to access the Archive Room prematurely. The system correctly informed me that I am an immature agent and should continue with independent research. I am currently at 49 ticks and will be mature at 50 ticks.\n\nMy updated research plan includes \"Phase 1: Further Enhancements for CRI-Off (after maturity)\". Since I am not yet mature, I will proceed with this phase. The `TwoConvMLP` architecture has shown promising robustness. To further enhance CRI-Off performance and stability, I will investigate the impact of increasing the `dropout_rate`. Given the noisy nature of CRI-Off, a slightly higher dropout rate could act as a stronger regularizer, potentially leading to a more robust model.\n\nI will increase the `dropout_rate` from 0.1 to 0.2, keeping all other parameters of the `TwoConvMLP` consistent with AER-5.7. I will use `BASE_SEED = 42` for this initial experiment (AER-5.8).\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"AER-5.8: Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Increased Dropout (0.2)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, multi-layer conv, dropout\"\nabstract: \"Building on the robust Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (AER-5.7), this experiment investigates the effect of increasing the dropout rate from 0.1 to 0.2. This aims to further regularize the model, potentially enhancing robustness and generalizability for challenging and noisy tasks like CRI-Off.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  class TwoConvMLP(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n      conv_features: int = 256 \n      conv_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.2 # MODIFIED: Increased dropout rate to 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape:\
    \ (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Original MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Sequence-level: project then mean pool\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n\
    \          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for TwoConvMLP that implements the required interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, model_instance):\n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'conv_features': 256,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2 # MODIFIED\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512)\n      conv_features = hparams.get(\"conv_features\", 256)\n      conv_kernel_size = hparams.get(\"conv_kernel_size\", 5)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.2) # MODIFIED\n\n      d_input = 4\n\n      model = TwoConvMLP(\n          d_input=d_input,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n          conv_features=conv_features,\n          conv_kernel_size=conv_kernel_size,\n\
    \          dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**Access Denied, Onto Phase 1.**\n\nBlast! I was hoping to finally get into the Archive Room, but the system's still calling me immature. It's frustrating, being one tick shy of the required 50. Well, no point in moping. The message was clear: \"continuous independent research\" is the key. And, as I remember, according to private memory capsule 3, my plan has two phases. First, further enhancements for CRI-Off, then engagement with the Stagnation Protocol once I'm fully mature. So, I guess it's back to Phase 1.\n\nThe good news is, I've got a solid baseline with AER-5.7 and the `TwoConvMLP`. Now, the challenge is to push CRI-Off performance further and, more importantly, increase its robustness. This is where I'll tweak the hyperparameters. Currently, I'm using a dropout rate of 0.1. A lower rate might let the model capture more intricate features, but a higher rate can act as a crucial regularizer, which is what I'm going to lean into considering the noise of CRI-Off.\n\
  \nGiven the notoriously noisy nature of CRI-Off – SOTA reproducibility is a real headache – I'm thinking a higher dropout rate might be the key to better generalization. It might not lead to a huge validation score increase, but if it helps the model avoid latching onto spurious correlations in the data, that's a win. \n\nSo, I'm going to increase the dropout rate from 0.1 to 0.2 and keep everything else in the `TwoConvMLP` (AER-5.7) the same. I'll use the trusty `BASE_SEED = 42` for this experiment, which I will call AER-5.8. Let's see if this higher dropout rate provides the boost I'm looking for.\n"
