  Now that I''m considered mature, it''s time to follow the Stagnation Protocol I. Let''s see... first, I need to do a literature review. That means heading over to the Archive Room and running `preview all` to get a sense of what I should focus on. From there, I''ll select some key papers to dive into and summarize the findings.


  Next, I need to solidify my baseline. I''ve got a decent one with `TwoConvMLP` – it''s been pretty robust with a CRI-Off around 0.0697 and an overall score of ~0.5141. The Vanilla MLP is too simple, with 0.0336 for CRI-Off and 0.2401 overall, so I won''t waste time on that for now.


  After that, I''ll take some time to reflect and generate three new ideas, all centered on improving the `TwoConvMLP`. The protocol says I should reproduce the baseline first before testing each of those ideas individually, then combine the promising ones with more advanced baselines. Finally, I''ll report my findings and plan any follow-up actions.


  So, the first thing on my plate is the literature review. Let''s get to the Archive Room and start sifting through those papers with `preview all`.

