tick: 489
role: model
parts:
- text: "Okay, let's refine the code structure for `create_network` and `_define_hyperparameters` to support these experimental ideas efficiently, especially the refactoring and conditional parameters for RegCal.\n\n**Refactoring for `create_network` and `_define_hyperparameters`:**\n\nTo support the modularity and conditional logic for RegCal and Adaptive Pooling, I'll need a more flexible `create_network` function that can instantiate the different head types and apply RegCal based on `hparams`.\n\nThe `TwoConvBackbone` will be a standalone Flax `nn.Module` that just processes the input sequence `x` and outputs `(batch, seq_len, conv_features)`.\n\nThe `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork` will then encapsulate:\n1.  Instantiation of `TwoConvBackbone`.\n2.  Application of global pooling (either fixed mean, or adaptive mean+max).\n3.  Conditional instantiation and application of the correct task-specific head (e.g., `RegressionHead`, `MultiLabelRegressionHead`, etc.).\n\nThe `RegressionHead` itself\
    \ will have the `l2_norm_input` and `dropout_rate` (for the head itself) as configurable parameters.\n\n**Revised `_define_hyperparameters` structure:**\n\nI will centralize all relevant hyperparameters in `_define_hyperparameters` and use `hparams.get()` with defaults in `create_network` to allow for easy toggling of features without rewriting the entire network definition.\n\n```python\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512, # For the dense layer after conv layers\n        'conv_features': 256,\n        'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Global dropout rate for backbone\n        'head_dense_dim': 128, # Intermediate dim for all prediction heads\n\n        # RegCal specific hparams\n        'use_regcal_l2': False, # Master switch for L2 normalization\n        'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.1, # Specific dropout for regression heads when RegCal is active\n\n        # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams\n\
    \        'use_adaptive_pooling': False,\n        'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64, # Intermediate dim for adaptive pooling gate\n    }\n```\n\n**Revised `create_network` structure (for the `TwoConvNetworkWrapper`):**\n\nThe `TwoConvNetworkWrapper` (which wraps `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork`) will be the primary object returned by `create_network`.\n\n```python\n# (RegressionHead, MultiLabelRegressionHead, MultiClassClassificationHead definitions as above,\n#  but now RegressionHead includes l2_norm_input and its own dropout_rate)\n\nclass TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    # ... (same as discussed, outputs (batch, seq_len, conv_features))\n    # It takes hparams for its internal config.\n\nclass TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n    # This module takes the full hparams dict and dynamically builds the network\n    # based on dataset-specific hparams (d_output, task_type, max_seq_len)\n    # and global hparams (dropout_rate, regcal_l2, adaptive_pooling etc.)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x, hparams, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone\n        backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n            conv_features=hparams['conv_features'],\n            conv_kernel_size=hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n            # hidden_dim applied within backbone if it has MLP part, or moved after pooling\n            # For current TwoConvMLP, it's after second conv layer, before final projection/pooling\n            hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n            name='two_conv_backbone'\n        )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, conv_features)\n\n        # 2. Global Pooling\n        if hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n            mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n            max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n            \n            combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n            gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(hparams['conv_features'],\
    \ name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled)\n            gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits)\n            pooled_features = gate_weights * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n        else:\n            pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # Default mean pooling\n\n        # 3. Task-Specific Heads\n        # Select head based on dataset-specific hparams\n        d_output = hparams['d_output'] # From dataset config\n        task_type = hparams['task_type'] # From dataset config\n        \n        if task_type == \"regression\":\n            head = RegressionHead(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                dense_dim=hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                dropout_rate=hparams['reg_head_dropout_rate'] if hparams['use_regcal_l2'] else hparams['dropout_rate'],\n                l2_norm_input=hparams['use_regcal_l2'],\n                name='regression_head'\n            )\n        elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n         \
    \   head = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                dense_dim=hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'], # No specific dropout for non-regression heads yet\n                name='multilabel_regression_head'\n            )\n        elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n            head = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                dense_dim=hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n                name='multilabel_classification_head'\n            )\n        elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n            head = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                dense_dim=hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n                name='multiclass_classification_head'\n            )\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown\
    \ task type: {task_type}\")\n\n        logits = head(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return logits\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    # This `create_network` wraps the main network with a `DSConvNetworkWrapper`\n    # and passes all hparams to the `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork`'s constructor or `__call__`\n    model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=hparams)\n    return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model) # The wrapper will pass hparams during init/apply\n```\n\n**Experimental Flow:**\n\n*   **AER-6.0 (Refactored Baseline):**\n    *   Set `use_regcal_l2 = False`, `use_adaptive_pooling = False`. `reg_head_dropout_rate` will default to `dropout_rate` (0.1).\n*   **AER-6.1 (L2 Normalization Only):**\n    *   Start from AER-6.0 code. Set `use_regcal_l2 = True`. `reg_head_dropout_rate` still matches `dropout_rate` (0.1). `use_adaptive_pooling = False`.\n*   **AER-6.2 (L2 Norm + Tailored Dropout):**\n    *   Start from AER-6.1 code. Set `use_regcal_l2 = True`, `reg_head_dropout_rate\
    \ = 0.05`. `use_adaptive_pooling = False`.\n*   **AER-6.3 (Adaptive Pooling Only):**\n    *   Start from AER-6.0 code. Set `use_regcal_l2 = False`, `use_adaptive_pooling = True`. `reg_head_dropout_rate` still matches `dropout_rate` (0.1).\n*   **AER-6.4 (Combined):**\n    *   Start from AER-6.0 code. Set `use_regcal_l2 = True`, `reg_head_dropout_rate = 0.05`, `use_adaptive_pooling = True`.\n\nThis systematic approach, controlled by `_define_hyperparameters` flags, should allow for clear isolation and evaluation of each new idea. The primary output of the `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork`'s `__call__` will take the `hparams` dict which includes both global model hparams and task-specific ones (like `d_output`, `task_type`). This matches the `create_network` interface.\n\nI also need to ensure that the `TwoConvBackbone` also passes its `hidden_dim` to the dense layer (if present) and `dropout_rate` to its internal dropout layers.\n\nThis detailed plan for the code structure and experiment flow\
    \ now feels solid. I am prepared for the next step: experimentation."
