tick: 490
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have completed my reflection session and have a clear plan for the next experiments. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement the refactored `TwoConvMLP` baseline (AER-6.0).\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-6.0: Refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Mean Pooling)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, baseline, CRI-Off, multi-layer conv, refactoring\"\nabstract: \"Establishment of a refactored 'Two Conv1D Layers Baseline' with explicit task-specific prediction heads, while maintaining the architectural and hyperparameter configuration of AER-5.7. This serves as a clean, modular foundation for subsequent experiments on Regression Calibration and Adaptive Pooling, ensuring a controlled environment for testing new ideas.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n\
    \  # These are now standalone and configurable\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False # Parameter for RegCal L2 norm\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6) # Add epsilon for stability\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n       \
    \   z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Backbone Architecture ---\n  class TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      conv_features: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x =\
    \ nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MLP layer after convolutions, before pooling\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='backbone_dense')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling ---\n  class TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any] # Pass all hparams here to configure sub-modules\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone\n          backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams['hidden_dim'],\n              conv_features=self.hparams['conv_features'],\n              conv_kernel_size=self.hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n\
    \              name='two_conv_backbone'\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (Mean Pooling for AER-6.0)\n          # In AER-6.0, use_adaptive_pooling is False\n          pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # Output: (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output'] # From dataset config\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type'] # From dataset config\n          \n          # All heads use the global dropout_rate for AER-6.0\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['dropout_rate'] \n          use_l2_norm = False # No RegCal L2 for AER-6.0\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n         \
    \         name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n  \
    \                dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface ---\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance, all_hparams):\n          self.network = model_instance\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams # Store all hparams for the apply method\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, self.all_hparams, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n \
    \         if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, self.all_hparams, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, self.all_hparams, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512, # Final dense layer size in backbone\n          'conv_features': 256, # Feature depth for Conv1D layers\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Global dropout rate (used for backbone and non-reg heads)\n          'head_dense_dim': 128, # Intermediate dense layer size for all prediction heads\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (set to False/default for AER-6.0)\n          'use_regcal_l2': False, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1, \n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (set to False for AER-6.0)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': False,\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64, \n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Combine global hparams with dataset-specific ones\n      # The main network expects a single hparams dict\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams) # Dataset-specific overrides (d_output, task_type, etc.)\n\n      model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams) # Pass all_hparams to wrapper for init/apply\n\n  # --- Optimizer Creation (Same as before) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Using a fixed seed for baseline verification\n\
    \  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**Immediate Priorities: AER-6.0 and the Stagnation Protocol**\n\nAlright, the reflection session is complete, and I'm back in the Chamber. Time to move forward. My next action is clear: AER-6.0, the refactored baseline, needs to be implemented in the Research Counter. That means `goto research` and then `submit` the code. Simple enough.\n\nWait, I should also make a note of this \"Station Announcement\" about Orion I's new archive capsule. While the Stagnation Protocol's \"Literature Review\" is conceptually finished, I'll need to keep it updated. It's a running process, and this new capsule is likely relevant. However, I have to prioritize. My planned experiment demands my immediate attention. AER-6.0 first. \n"
