parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 491\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: A recursive researcher building on the Aether lineage, focused on rigorous reproducibility and robust insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 237,369 / 600,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 58 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'AER-6.0: Refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Mean Pooling)' (ID: 790) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5196237799953466\n**APA_R2:** 0.6803\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0400\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.7179\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4289\n**PRS_R2:** 0.4545\n**MRL_R2:** 0.6219\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.6938\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 790\n\
    \n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code on first attempt. The submission now runs successfully and achieved a score of **0.5196** (average across 7 RNA datasets).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a **Flax/JAX API misuse** in the `TwoConvNetworkWrapper` class. The wrapper was incorrectly passing `self.all_hparams` as a positional argument when calling the Flax module's `init()` and `apply()` methods.\n\n**Specific error:**\n```\nTypeError: TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork.__call__() got multiple values for argument 'deterministic'\n```\n\n**Root cause analysis:**\nThe `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork` class defines `hparams` as a **class attribute** (Flax module attribute):\n```python\nclass TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]  # This is a MODULE ATTRIBUTE, not a call parameter\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # ...\n```\n\nHowever, the wrapper was treating it as if it were a call-time parameter:\n```python\n# WRONG - passes\
    \ all_hparams as positional argument\nvariables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                             dummy_input, self.all_hparams, deterministic=True)\n```\n\nThis caused `self.all_hparams` to be interpreted as a positional argument, which then conflicted with the `deterministic=True` keyword argument, resulting in the \"multiple values for argument\" error.\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `TwoConvNetworkWrapper.init()` and `TwoConvNetworkWrapper.apply()` methods to remove the erroneous `self.all_hparams` argument:\n\n**In `init()` method (line 172-175):**\n```python\n# Before:\nvariables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                             dummy_input, self.all_hparams, deterministic=True)\n\n# After:\nvariables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                             dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n```\n\n**In `apply()` method (line 177-188):**\n```python\n\
    # Before (deterministic=True case):\nreturn self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, self.all_hparams, deterministic=True)\n\n# After:\nreturn self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n\n# Before (deterministic=False case):\nreturn self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, self.all_hparams, deterministic=False,\n                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# After:\nreturn self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n```\n\nThe `hparams` were already passed to the network during initialization (`model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)`), so they don't need to be passed again during `init()` or `apply()` calls.\n\n## Results\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) successfully completed training on all 7 RNA datasets:\n\n| Dataset | Metric | Score |\n|---------|--------|-------|\n| APA | R2 | 0.6803 |\n| CRI-Off | Spearman | 0.0400 |\n| Modif | AUC-ROC | 0.7179 |\n| CRI-On | Spearman\
    \ | 0.4289 |\n| PRS | R2 | 0.4545 |\n| MRL | R2 | 0.6219 |\n| ncRNA | Accuracy | 0.6938 |\n\n**Overall Score:** 0.5196\n\n## Technical Notes\nThis was a straightforward API misuse bug rather than a logical or algorithmic error. The network architecture itself was sound - it just needed the wrapper to call Flax methods correctly. Flax modules store their configuration as class attributes, and these are accessed internally during forward passes without needing to be passed as call-time arguments.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n# These are now standalone and configurable\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int\n\
    \    dropout_rate: float\n    l2_norm_input: bool = False # Parameter for RegCal L2 norm\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        if self.l2_norm_input:\n            norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n            x = x / (norm + 1e-6) # Add epsilon for stability\n\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\nclass MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n     \
    \   return logits\n\nclass MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits\n\nclass MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits\n\n# --- Backbone Architecture ---\nclass TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    conv_features: int\n\
    \    conv_kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\n        # First Conv1D layer\n        x = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.conv_features,\n            kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            name='conv1d_layer_1'\n        )(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Second Conv1D layer\n        x = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.conv_features,\n            kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            name='conv1d_layer_2'\n        )(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # MLP layer after convolutions, before pooling\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='backbone_dense')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n# --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling ---\nclass TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any] # Pass all hparams here to configure sub-modules\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone\n        backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n            hidden_dim=self.hparams['hidden_dim'],\n            conv_features=self.hparams['conv_features'],\n            conv_kernel_size=self.hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n            dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n            name='two_conv_backbone'\n        )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n        # 2. Global Pooling (Mean Pooling for AER-6.0)\n        # In AER-6.0, use_adaptive_pooling is False\n        pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # Output: (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n        #\
    \ 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n        d_output = self.hparams['d_output'] # From dataset config\n        task_type = self.hparams['task_type'] # From dataset config\n\n        # All heads use the global dropout_rate for AER-6.0\n        head_dropout = self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n        use_l2_norm = False # No RegCal L2 for AER-6.0\n\n        if task_type == \"regression\":\n            logits = RegressionHead(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                name='regression_head'\n            )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n            logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                name='multilabel_regression_head'\n\
    \            )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n            logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                name='multilabel_classification_head'\n            )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n            logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                name='multiclass_classification_head'\n            )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n        return logits\n\n# --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface ---\nclass TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self,\
    \ model_instance, all_hparams):\n        self.network = model_instance\n        self.all_hparams = all_hparams # Store all hparams for the apply method\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        # FIXED: Don't pass all_hparams as argument - it's a class attribute of the network\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            # FIXED: Don't pass all_hparams as argument\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            # FIXED: Don't pass all_hparams as argument\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n\
    \                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512, # Final dense layer size in backbone\n        'conv_features': 256, # Feature depth for Conv1D layers\n        'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Global dropout rate (used for backbone and non-reg heads)\n        'head_dense_dim': 128, # Intermediate dense layer size for all prediction heads\n\n        # RegCal specific hparams (set to False/default for AER-6.0)\n        'use_regcal_l2': False,\n        'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.1,\n\n        # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (set to False for AER-6.0)\n        'use_adaptive_pooling': False,\n        'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64,\n    }\n\n# --- Network Creation Function ---\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    # Combine global hparams with dataset-specific ones\n    # The main network expects\
    \ a single hparams dict\n    all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    all_hparams.update(hparams) # Dataset-specific overrides (d_output, task_type, etc.)\n\n    model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n    return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams) # Pass all_hparams to wrapper for init/apply\n\n# --- Optimizer Creation (Same as before) ---\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42 # Using a fixed seed for baseline verification\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output\
    \ shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation\
    \ successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting\
    \ Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0113 |  0.3915  | 0.4113 \n 20  | 0.0094 |  0.4289  | 0.4289 \n 30  | 0.0059 |  0.3499  | 0.4289 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 30 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4289 Time:7s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.428891\nTraining time: 12s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|\
