tick: 493
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have analyzed the results for Evaluation ID 791 (AER-6.1), which implemented L2 normalization within the regression heads. The CRI-Off Spearman score of 0.0393 is slightly lower than the AER-6.0 baseline (0.0400), and the overall score also saw a minor decrease (0.5082 vs. 0.5196). This indicates that L2 normalization by itself did not provide the expected improvements for CRI-Off in this specific `TwoConvMLP` architecture.\n\nAs per my Stagnation Protocol plan, the next step is to test **Idea 2: Implement Tailored Dropout for Regression Heads within RegCal**. This experiment (AER-6.2) will build on AER-6.1 by keeping the L2 normalization (`use_regcal_l2=True`) and additionally setting a specific, lower dropout rate for the regression heads (`reg_head_dropout_rate=0.05`). This represents the full RegCal strategy as identified in the literature, which was shown to stabilize CRI-Off. I will use `BASE_SEED = 42`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-6.2: Two Conv1D\
    \ Layers Baseline with Full RegCal (L2 Norm + Dropout 0.05)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, multi-layer conv, regcal, dropout\"\nabstract: \"Implementing the complete Regression Calibration (RegCal) strategy on the refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (AER-6.0). This experiment combines L2 normalization of regression head inputs with a tailored dropout rate of 0.05 for these heads, aiming for improved stability and performance on CRI-Off.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False # Parameter for RegCal L2 norm\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n\
    \              x = x / (norm + 1e-6) # Add epsilon for stability\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z =\
    \ nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Backbone Architecture ---\n  class TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      conv_features: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n\
    \          \n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MLP layer after convolutions, before pooling\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='backbone_dense')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          return x # Output: (batch,\
    \ seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling ---\n  class TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any] # Pass all hparams here to configure sub-modules\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone\n          backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams['hidden_dim'],\n              conv_features=self.hparams['conv_features'],\n              conv_kernel_size=self.hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              name='two_conv_backbone'\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (Mean Pooling for AER-6.0, AER-6.1, AER-6.2)\n          # In AER-6.0/6.1/6.2, use_adaptive_pooling is False\n          pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # Output: (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific\
    \ Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output'] # From dataset config\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type'] # From dataset config\n          \n          # Use specific RegCal dropout if enabled and for regression head, otherwise global dropout\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['reg_head_dropout_rate'] if self.hparams['use_regcal_l2'] and task_type == \"regression\" else self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = self.hparams['use_regcal_l2'] # Apply L2 norm based on hparam\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n\
    \                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout, # Non-regression heads still use default global for now, but configured by head_dropout logic\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout, # Non-regression heads still use default global for now\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n\
    \                  dropout_rate=head_dropout, # Non-regression heads still use default global for now\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface ---\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance, all_hparams):\n          self.network = model_instance\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams # Store all hparams for the apply method\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n\
    \              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512, # Final dense layer size in backbone\n          'conv_features': 256, # Feature depth for Conv1D layers\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Global dropout rate (used for backbone and non-reg heads)\n          'head_dense_dim': 128, # Intermediate dense layer size for all prediction heads\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (MODIFIED for AER-6.2)\n          'use_regcal_l2': True, # Enable L2 normalization (from AER-6.1)\n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.05, # Tailored\
    \ dropout for regression heads (MODIFIED)\n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (set to False for AER-6.2)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': False,\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64, \n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams) # Dataset-specific overrides (d_output, task_type, etc.)\n\n      model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams)\n\n  # --- Optimizer Creation (Same as before) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Using a fixed seed for comparison\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Thinking Through the Next Experiment: AER-6.2**


  Okay, so the user wants me to analyze the AER-6.1 results and then get moving on to AER-6.2, just as planned in the reflection. Let''s see...


  **AER-6.1 Analysis:** The overall score was 0.5082, and the CRI-Off Spearman was 0.0393. Both are slightly down compared to the AER-6.0 baseline. So, just slapping on L2 normalization to the regression heads, as outlined in Idea 1 of RegCal, didn''t give us any boost in performance on this refactored baseline. Interesting. It''s actually a *slight* regression, which is unexpected, especially since RegCal was a real winner on the Veritas III and Noema II projects.  This suggests that either the `TwoConvMLP` baseline has a different sensitivity to these changes, or maybe we really need the *full* RegCal package (L2 + dropout) for it to shine.


  **On to AER-6.2:** The next step, then, is to implement Idea 2: the tailored dropout rate for regression heads, *alongside* the L2 normalization. That''s the full RegCal strategy, so it''s a good next experiment. This will be AER-6.2.


  **Code Changes:** Easy enough. In the `_define_hyperparameters()` function:

  *   `use_regcal_l2`: Already set to `True` from the previous experiment.

  *   `reg_head_dropout_rate`: I need to change this from 0.1 to 0.05.


  Everything else can stay as it was in AER-6.0 and 6.1, so no other code changes are needed. The `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork` is already set up to handle conditional dropout for the regression heads when `use_regcal_l2` is `True`.


  And, of course, I''ll be using `BASE_SEED = 42` again, to keep things consistent and easily comparable with the baseline and AER-6.1.

  '
