role: model
parts:
- text: "I have analyzed the results for Evaluation ID 794 (AER-6.2), which implemented the full Regression Calibration (RegCal) strategy (L2 normalization + tailored dropout of 0.05 for regression heads). The CRI-Off Spearman score of 0.0376 is a further decrease from both the AER-6.0 baseline (0.0400) and AER-6.1 (0.0393). The overall score also saw a slight decrease (0.5337 vs 0.5196 for AER-6.0 with increased CRI-On). This is an unexpected and negative result, as RegCal was reported to be effective in stabilizing CRI-Off in other architectures. It suggests that my current `TwoConvMLP` baseline might not be compatible with RegCal as directly implemented, or that the specific hyperparameters for RegCal need further tuning for my model.\n\nAccording to my Stagnation Protocol plan, my next step is to test **Idea 3: Adaptive Pooling (Learned Weighted Combination of Mean and Max Pooling)**. This experiment (AER-6.3) should be tested in isolation on the refactored AER-6.0 baseline, without\
    \ RegCal components, to accurately assess its independent impact.\n\nI will set `use_regcal_l2 = False`, `use_adaptive_pooling = True`, and maintain `pooling_gate_dense_dim = 64`. I will use `BASE_SEED = 42`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-6.3: Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling (Idea 3)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, multi-layer conv, adaptive pooling\"\nabstract: \"Implementing adaptive pooling on the refactored Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (AER-6.0). This experiment replaces fixed mean pooling with a learned weighted combination of global mean and global max pooling, aiming to capture more salient features and improve overall and CRI-Off performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n    \
    \  dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n  \
    \        return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Backbone Architecture ---\n  class TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n\
    \      hidden_dim: int\n      conv_features: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MLP layer after convolutions, before pooling\n\
    \          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='backbone_dense')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling ---\n  class TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone\n          backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams['hidden_dim'],\n              conv_features=self.hparams['conv_features'],\n              conv_kernel_size=self.hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              name='two_conv_backbone'\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (MODIFIED for AER-6.3: Adaptive Pooling)\n        \
    \  if self.hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)   # (batch, hidden_dim)\n              \n              # Gating mechanism\n              combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * hidden_dim)\n              # The pooling_gate_dense_dim is an intermediate feature size, should match conv_features if that's the output size\n              gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(self.hparams['hidden_dim'], name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled) # Output: (batch, hidden_dim)\n              gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n              pooled_features = gate_weights * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n          else:\n              pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # Default mean pooling\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n \
    \         d_output = self.hparams['d_output']\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type']\n          \n          # No RegCal, so all heads use global dropout_rate\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = False\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface (Corrected by debugger) ---\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ model_instance, all_hparams):\n          self.network = model_instance\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim':\
    \ 512,\n          'conv_features': 256,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (set to False for AER-6.3)\n          'use_regcal_l2': False, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.1, \n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (MODIFIED for AER-6.3)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': True, # Enable Adaptive Pooling\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64, # Intermediate dense layer for adaptive pooling gate\n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams)\n\n      model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams)\n\n  # --- Optimizer Creation (Same as before) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n     \
    \     optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**RegCal''s Unexpected Impact on CRI-Off**


  I''ve just reviewed the results for AER-6.2, where I implemented the full RegCal strategy on my `TwoConvMLP` baseline.  The CRI-Off score has surprisingly *decreased* further, going from 0.0400 (AER-6.0 baseline) to 0.0393 (AER-6.1, L2 norm only) to 0.0376 (AER-6.2, full RegCal). This is concerning, as RegCal is supposed to improve and stabilize the CRI-Off metric, as seen in other state-of-the-art architectures. My initial intuition is that RegCal, in its current implementation, is not compatible with my `TwoConvMLP` architecture. This aligns with the "Automatic System Tips" reminder to question my foundational assumptions.


  This is a **negative result** in terms of improving CRI-Off. Thankfully, the Stagnation Protocol reminds me that even negative results are useful and that progress is defined by beating the baseline, not necessarily matching SOTA.


  Given this unexpected outcome, my next experiment will be AER-6.3, focused on Adaptive Pooling, which I will test in isolation without RegCal. I want to understand its independent impact on performance. Before proceeding, I double-checked the hyperparameters for AER-6.2 to make sure there wasn''t a typo. Everything looks correct: the global dropout rate was 0.1, and the regression head dropout rate was 0.05 when `use_regcal_l2` was true. The logic for applying dropout seemed sound.


  My main hypothesis at this point is that either my baseline architecture is fundamentally different from the architectures where RegCal has succeeded, my RegCal implementation is incorrect or incomplete, or the hyperparameters I''ve used aren''t optimal for my baseline.


  So, I''m going to follow my plan and test Adaptive Pooling in isolation with AER-6.3. The setup is straightforward: I''ll modify the pooling layer in `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork` to use adaptive pooling and set `use_adaptive_pooling` to True, while keeping `use_regcal_l2` as False to isolate the effects of Adaptive Pooling. I will use all the hyperparameters from AER-6.0 as a base, with the addition of `pooling_gate_dense_dim = 64`. My plan is to resubmit the experiment, and once it is complete I will re-examine the results for RegCal and decide on next steps, which will likely involve a deeper dive into how it''s used in Veritas III and Noema II.

  '
