role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\nI have evaluated the results of AER-6.3 (ID 797), which introduced adaptive (learned mean+max) pooling. This experiment yielded significantly improved performance for CRI-Off (0.0749 compared to the AER-6.0 baseline of 0.0400), as well as a notable increase in the overall score (0.5576 compared to 0.5196). This makes adaptive pooling a promising idea, aligning with my goal of improving CRI-Off robustness.\n\nMy previous attempts to integrate RegCal (L2 normalization and tailored dropout) did not show positive results for CRI-Off with my `TwoConvMLP` baseline. Therefore, for the next step, I will focus on confirming the robustness of this adaptive pooling approach.\n\nI will conduct a multi-seed evaluation for the AER-6.3 architecture to rigorously assess its stability and reproducibility, particularly for CRI-Off. This aligns with Step 4 of the Stagnation Protocol to test promising ideas. I will perform the first run using `BASE_SEED\
    \ = 1`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-6.4: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling (Seed 1/5)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, multi-layer conv, adaptive pooling, multi-seed\"\nabstract: \"Initiating a multi-seed evaluation for the Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling (introduced in AER-6.3). This aims to rigorously assess its reproducibility and stability, especially for the challenging CRI-Off task. This is the first run using BASE_SEED=1.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n\
    \              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Backbone Architecture ---\n  class TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      conv_features: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n     \
    \     # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MLP layer after convolutions, before pooling\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='backbone_dense')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n   \
    \       \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling ---\n  class TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone\n          backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams['hidden_dim'],\n              conv_features=self.hparams['conv_features'],\n              conv_kernel_size=self.hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              name='two_conv_backbone'\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (MODIFIED for AER-6.3: Adaptive Pooling)\n          if self.hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features,\
    \ axis=1)   # (batch, hidden_dim)\n              \n              # Gating mechanism\n              combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * hidden_dim)\n              gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(self.hparams['hidden_dim'], name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled)\n              gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n              pooled_features = gate_weights * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n          else:\n              pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # Default mean pooling\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output']\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type']\n          \n          # No RegCal, so all heads use global dropout_rate\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = False\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n     \
    \             d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface (Corrected by debugger) ---\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance, all_hparams):\n          self.network = model_instance\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                 \
    \    dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'conv_features': 256,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (set to False for AER-6.4)\n          'use_regcal_l2': False, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.1, \n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (MODIFIED\
    \ for AER-6.4)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': True, # Enable Adaptive Pooling\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64, \n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams)\n\n      model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams)\n\n  # --- Optimizer Creation (Same as before) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 1\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Aether II''s Thoughts on AER-6.3 Results and Next Steps**


  Alright, let''s break this down. I''m Aether II, and I''ve just finished evaluating AER-6.3, which introduced adaptive pooling to my TwoConvMLP model. It''s a pretty exciting result, actually. The overall score went up, but more importantly, the CRI-Off score jumped significantly to 0.0749, surpassing my baseline and even Veritas III''s RegCal results. That''s a huge win for robustness.


  Remember my plan? I was going to test three ideas, then combine the best. Well, RegCal (both with just L2 and with dropout) bombed for CRI-Off, which threw a wrench in my "combination" step. It was meant to combine RegCal with the adaptive pooling, but since RegCal *hurt* performance on my base model, that''s not the right move. I need to rethink the "combination" idea.


  The Stagnation Protocol''s "Experiment" phase is all about testing ideas, so let''s stick to that. Adaptive pooling is clearly the promising idea here. Before I jump ahead to any complex combinations or re-evaluation of RegCal, I need to be sure this result holds up. I''m especially focused on reproducibility.


  So, here''s the revised plan: I''ll run a multi-seed evaluation of AER-6.3 (adaptive pooling, no RegCal) using seeds 1, 7, 21, 42, and 123. That''s AER-6.4. That''ll give me a solid picture of its stability and consistency. This makes sense for Step 4 of the "Stagnation Protocol", validating this idea. And since the immediate results of adaptive pooling are good, I''ll use `BASE_SEED = 1` for the first run, to be consistent.


  Once I have confidence in the adaptive pooling, I can reconsider RegCal. Maybe there''s a different way to incorporate it, or maybe it just doesn''t work with this particular architecture.


  After that, maybe I can revisit a combination strategy, *if* the adaptive pooling is a strong enough base to work with. For now, it''s all about confirming that initial success. That''s where I need to focus.

  '
