role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\nI have analyzed the results for Evaluation ID 803 (AER-6.4, Seed 1). The overall score of 0.5595 and the CRI-Off Spearman correlation of 0.0770 represent a consistent improvement over my refactored baseline (AER-6.0: overall 0.5196, CRI-Off 0.0400). This further validates adaptive pooling as a promising enhancement for both overall performance and CRI-Off robustness.\n\nAs per my Stagnation Protocol plan to rigorously test promising ideas, I will continue the multi-seed evaluation for the `TwoConvMLP` architecture with adaptive pooling. The next run will use `BASE_SEED = 7`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-6.4: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling (Seed 7/5)\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, multi-layer conv, adaptive pooling, multi-seed\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the multi-seed evaluation for the Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling\
    \ (introduced in AER-6.3). This is the second run, using BASE_SEED=7, to assess its reproducibility and stability, particularly for the challenging CRI-Off task.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\
    \n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n\
    \      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Backbone Architecture ---\n  class TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      conv_features: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          \n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MLP layer after convolutions, before pooling\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='backbone_dense')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling ---\n  class TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone\n          backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams['hidden_dim'],\n\
    \              conv_features=self.hparams['conv_features'],\n              conv_kernel_size=self.hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              name='two_conv_backbone'\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (MODIFIED for AER-6.3: Adaptive Pooling)\n          if self.hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)   # (batch, hidden_dim)\n              \n              # Gating mechanism\n              combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * hidden_dim)\n              gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(self.hparams['hidden_dim'], name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled)\n              gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n              pooled_features\
    \ = gate_weights * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n          else:\n              pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # Default mean pooling\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output']\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type']\n          \n          # No RegCal, so all heads use global dropout_rate\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = False\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n\
    \                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n\
    \              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface (Corrected by debugger) ---\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance, all_hparams):\n          self.network = model_instance\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n\
    \                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'conv_features': 256,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (set to False for AER-6.4)\n          'use_regcal_l2': False, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.1, \n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (MODIFIED for AER-6.4)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': True, # Enable Adaptive Pooling\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64, \n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams)\n\n      model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams)\n\n  # --- Optimizer\
    \ Creation (Same as before) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analysis of AER-6.4 (Seed 1) and Next Steps**


  Alright, let''s take stock. I''m Aether II, here in the Research Counter, just got the results back for AER-6.4 (ID 803), my multi-seed evaluation of Adaptive Pooling, and the initial results are quite encouraging. Let''s dig in.


  The overall score of 0.5595 and the CRI-Off Spearman of 0.0770 are a solid leap forward. It''s noticeably better than the refactored baseline (AER-6.0) at 0.5196/0.0400, and even edges out the earlier pre-refactor TwoConvMLP (AER-5.7) with its mean scores. My previous single run of Adaptive Pooling (AER-6.3) was showing promise with 0.5576/0.0749, and AER-6.4 is tracking this, also.  The CRI-Off, in particular, is looking robust, better than the baseline and pre-refactor. This is exactly what I was hoping to see.


  Now, as per the Stagnation Protocol, I''m currently at Step 4.  I''ve already tested RegCal L2 Norm and Full RegCal, and neither of them proved to move the needle on CRI-Off. However, Adaptive Pooling, Idea 3, is looking promising. I''m in the middle of a multi-seed evaluation (AER-6.4) and need to see how the other seeds perform to confirm reproducibility and understand the variation.


  I need to nail down the stability of this technique before I consider combining it with other ideas. The focus here is to make sure this is a real effect and not just a fluke. So, I will now run the second seed of AER-6.4 using `BASE_SEED = 7`. After that, I will assess the results of the full multi-seed evaluation. If it holds, I can consider combining Adaptive Pooling with other modifications in AER-6.5.

  '
