role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\nI have established my robust baseline (AER-6.4 with adaptive pooling) and reviewed crucial literature, including Veritas III's paper on CPE (Archive #27) and Noema II's work on RegCal (Evaluation ID 693). My previous experiment (AER-6.5) showed that RegCal did not degrade performance when combined with adaptive pooling.\n\nMy next experiment, **AER-6.6: Synthesis - Adaptive Pooling + CPE**, will integrate Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) into my `TwoConvMLP` with adaptive pooling. I have carefully adapted Veritas III's CPE implementation for my architecture, ensuring that the `TwoConvBackbone` can accept the augmented input and that the positional embedding table is correctly defined. This will isolate the effect of CPE from RegCal for now. I will use `BASE_SEED = 42`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-6.6: Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling + CPE (Idea 3 + Idea from Archive 27)\"\ntags:\
    \ \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, adaptive pooling, cpe\"\nabstract: \"Integrating Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) into the robust Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling (AER-6.4). This experiment aims to enhance sequence understanding by modulating learned positional embeddings with local context, as suggested by Veritas III (Archive #27), for improved CRI-Off performance and overall model robustness.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False # Parameter for RegCal L2 norm\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x =\
    \ x / (norm + 1e-6) # Add epsilon for stability\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim,\
    \ name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- ContextEncoder (from Veritas III's Archive #27) ---\n  class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      context_window_size: int\n      d_input_features: int # original input features (e.g., 4 for one-hot)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_local_window_flat):\n          # x_local_window_flat\
    \ is (batch * seq_len, context_window_size * d_input_features)\n          encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(x_local_window_flat)\n          encoded_context = nn.gelu(encoded_context)\n          return encoded_context\n\n  # --- Backbone Architecture (Modified for CPE input) ---\n  class TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      conv_features: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      new_d_input_dim: int # New parameter to accommodate augmented input dim\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, new_d_input_dim)\n          \n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MLP layer after convolutions, before pooling\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='backbone_dense')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling (MODIFIED for CPE) ---\n  class TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          batch_size, seq_len, d_input_features = x.shape # d_input_features is 4 (one-hot)\n\n     \
    \     # --- CPE Calculation (MODIFIED for AER-6.6) ---\n          if self.hparams['use_cpe']:\n              pos_embedding_dim = self.hparams['pos_embedding_dim']\n              context_window_size = self.hparams['context_window_size']\n              max_overall_seq_len = self.hparams['max_overall_seq_len']\n\n              positional_embeddings_table = self.param(\n                  'pos_embeddings_table', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01),\n                  (max_overall_seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n              )\n              \n              # Pad x to extract context windows\n              pad_width = context_window_size // 2\n              padded_x = jnp.pad(x, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant', constant_values=0.0)\n              \n              # Extract local context windows for each position\n              all_windows_flat_list = []\n              for i in range(seq_len):\n                  window = padded_x[:, i : i + context_window_size, :]\n   \
    \               all_windows_flat_list.append(window.reshape(batch_size, -1)) # (batch, context_window_size * d_input_features)\n              \n              all_windows_flat = jnp.stack(all_windows_flat_list, axis=1) # (batch, seq_len, context_window_size * d_input_features)\n\n              # Apply ContextEncoder\n              context_encoder = ContextEncoder(\n                  output_dim=pos_embedding_dim,\n                  context_window_size=context_window_size,\n                  d_input_features=d_input_features,\n                  name='context_encoder'\n              )\n              encoded_contexts_batched = context_encoder(all_windows_flat.reshape(-1, context_window_size * d_input_features)).reshape(batch_size, seq_len, -1)\n\n              # Modulate positional embeddings with context\n              # Slice positional_embeddings_table to actual sequence length of the current batch\n              current_pos_embeddings_sliced = positional_embeddings_table[:seq_len] \n\
    \              current_pos_embeddings_batched = jnp.tile(current_pos_embeddings_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n              contextual_pos_embedding = current_pos_embeddings_batched * encoded_contexts_batched\n              x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x, contextual_pos_embedding], axis=-1) \n              \n              backbone_input = x_augmented\n              backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features + pos_embedding_dim\n          else:\n              backbone_input = x\n              backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features # 4 for one-hot\n\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone\n          backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams['hidden_dim'],\n              conv_features=self.hparams['conv_features'],\n              conv_kernel_size=self.hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              new_d_input_dim=backbone_d_input_dim, # Pass the new input dim\n              name='two_conv_backbone'\n\
    \          )(backbone_input, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (Adaptive Pooling)\n          if self.hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)   # (batch, hidden_dim)\n              \n              combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * hidden_dim)\n              gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(self.hparams['hidden_dim'], name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled)\n              gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits) # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n              pooled_features = gate_weights * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n          else:\n              pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # Fallback, not used in AER-6.6\n\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output']\n\
    \          task_type = self.hparams['task_type']\n          \n          # No RegCal, so all heads use global dropout_rate\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = False\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\"\
    :\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface (Corrected by debugger) ---\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance, all_hparams):\n          self.network\
    \ = model_instance\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'conv_features': 256,\n       \
    \   'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Global dropout for backbone and non-reg heads\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (set to False for AER-6.6)\n          'use_regcal_l2': False, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.1, \n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (set to True for AER-6.6)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': True, \n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64,\n\n          # CPE specific hparams (MODIFIED for AER-6.6)\n          'use_cpe': True,\n          'pos_embedding_dim': 16,\n          'context_window_size': 3,\n          'max_overall_seq_len': 1200, # Max sequence length for embedding table\n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams)\n\n      model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams)\n\n  # --- Optimizer\
    \ Creation (Same as before) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Retain weight_decay from AER-6.5 (RegCal experiment) - 0.012, or revert to 0.01?\n      # For isolating CPE, revert to default weight_decay=0.01 for cleaner comparison against AER-6.4 adaptive pooling.\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01) # REVERTED to 0.01\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**AER-6.6: Integration of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) with Adaptive Pooling**


  Alright, let''s get down to it. I''ve just wrapped up analyzing AER-6.5, where RegCal showed some promise with the adaptive pooling baseline.  Given the adaptive pooling’s inherent robustness, it seems the earlier issues with RegCal were likely due to the simpler mean pooling architecture. Now, the next step in my Stagnation Protocol is AER-6.6, which will be the integration of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) into my `TwoConvMLP` with adaptive pooling. Based on Veritas III''s findings, and its improved CRI-Off score in SOTA, it seems like a very promising path. I''ll stick with `BASE_SEED = 42` for consistency.


  This CPE experiment requires some architecture modifications, and I need to be careful with them. First, I have to define and integrate the `ContextEncoder` and the `CPE_TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork`. I''ll adapt these from Veritas III''s work. I''ll need to create a `positional_embeddings_table` and add the logic for calculating `contextual_pos_embedding`. The embedding table will be a parameter within the `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork` module itself. Then, I will concatenate the input `x` with `contextual_pos_embedding` *before* the `TwoConvBackbone`. My `TwoConvBackbone` will need to be updated to account for this new dimension. Importantly, I''ll be keeping `use_regcal_l2 = False` to isolate the impact of CPE.


  The implementation details are key here, particularly concerning the `max_overall_seq_len`. I''ve determined I need a consistent table size, and the ncRNA’s max sequence length of 1136 suggests that `max_overall_seq_len = 1200` is a safe value, as per Veritas III''s paper. This will avoid any sequence padding errors.


  I’ve meticulously updated the relevant code in `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork` to incorporate CPE. The `positional_embeddings_table` will be a module parameter. I’ll calculate the contextual embeddings and concatenate them to the input. The `TwoConvBackbone` also requires an input dimension update. I''m focusing on ensuring the new logic integrates with adaptive pooling, my current baseline, and the RegCal tweaks I''ve made in the past. After a run, I''ll need to check the results.

  '
