role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\nI have just analyzed the results of AER-6.6 (Evaluation ID 821), which integrated Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) with my adaptive pooling `TwoConvMLP` architecture. The overall score of 0.6325 is a significant improvement over both my refactored mean-pooling baseline (AER-6.0: 0.5196) and my adaptive pooling baseline (AER-6.4 mean: ~0.5585). Crucially, the CRI-Off Spearman score of 0.0741 maintains the robust and stable performance observed with adaptive pooling (mean ~0.0739, Std Dev ~0.0025). This confirms CPE as a highly promising idea.\n\nMy previous re-evaluation of RegCal (AER-6.5) showed that it did not degrade performance when combined with adaptive pooling, although it didn't provide a significant boost either. Given that RegCal has proven effective in other lineages' complex architectures, it's worth testing the ultimate synergy.\n\nTherefore, as per my Stagnation Protocol plan, I will now proceed with **AER-6.7:\
    \ Synergistic Synthesis - Adaptive Pooling + RegCal + CPE**. This experiment will combine my most robust `TwoConvMLP` with adaptive pooling, the full RegCal strategy (L2 normalization + tailored dropout of 0.05 for regression heads and `weight_decay=0.012`), and Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE). This aims to unlock a new level of performance and robustness, especially for CRI-Off.\n\nI will use `BASE_SEED = 42` for this initial run.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-6.7: Two Conv1D Layers Baseline with Adaptive Pooling + Full RegCal + CPE\"\ntags: \"conv1d, mlp, robustness, CRI-Off, adaptive pooling, regcal, cpe, synthesis\"\nabstract: \"This experiment represents a synergistic synthesis of three promising ideas: Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling, the complete Regression Calibration (RegCal) strategy, and Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE), integrated into the Two Conv1D Layers Baseline. This aims to achieve breakthrough stability and performance, particularly\
    \ for the challenging CRI-Off task, by combining proven architectural enhancements and regularization techniques.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False # Parameter for RegCal L2 norm\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6) # Add epsilon for stability\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\
    \n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n\
    \      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- ContextEncoder (from Veritas III's Archive #27) ---\n  class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      context_window_size: int\n      d_input_features: int # original input features (e.g., 4 for one-hot)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_local_window_flat):\n          # x_local_window_flat is (batch * seq_len, context_window_size * d_input_features)\n          encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(x_local_window_flat)\n          encoded_context = nn.gelu(encoded_context)\n          return encoded_context\n\n  # --- Backbone Architecture (Modified for CPE input) ---\n\
    \  class TwoConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      conv_features: int\n      conv_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      new_d_input_dim: int # New parameter to accommodate augmented input dim\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, new_d_input_dim)\n          \n          # First Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Second Conv1D layer\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.conv_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv1d_layer_2'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MLP layer after convolutions, before pooling\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='backbone_dense')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling (MODIFIED for CPE) ---\n  class TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          batch_size, seq_len, d_input_features = x.shape # d_input_features is 4 (one-hot)\n\n          # --- CPE Calculation ---\n          if self.hparams['use_cpe']:\n              pos_embedding_dim = self.hparams['pos_embedding_dim']\n              context_window_size = self.hparams['context_window_size']\n              max_overall_seq_len = self.hparams['max_overall_seq_len']\n\n              positional_embeddings_table\
    \ = self.param(\n                  'pos_embeddings_table', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01),\n                  (max_overall_seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n              )\n              \n              # Pad x to extract context windows\n              pad_width = context_window_size // 2\n              padded_x = jnp.pad(x, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant', constant_values=0.0)\n              \n              # Extract local context windows for each position\n              all_windows_flat_list = []\n              for i in range(seq_len):\n                  window = padded_x[:, i : i + context_window_size, :]\n                  all_windows_flat_list.append(window.reshape(batch_size, -1))\n              \n              all_windows_flat = jnp.stack(all_windows_flat_list, axis=1)\n\n              # Apply ContextEncoder\n              context_encoder = ContextEncoder(\n                  output_dim=pos_embedding_dim,\n                  context_window_size=context_window_size,\n\
    \                  d_input_features=d_input_features,\n                  name='context_encoder'\n              )\n              encoded_contexts_batched = context_encoder(all_windows_flat.reshape(-1, context_window_size * d_input_features)).reshape(batch_size, seq_len, -1)\n\n              # Modulate positional embeddings with context\n              current_pos_embeddings_sliced = positional_embeddings_table[:seq_len] \n              current_pos_embeddings_batched = jnp.tile(current_pos_embeddings_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n              contextual_pos_embedding = current_pos_embeddings_batched * encoded_contexts_batched\n              x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x, contextual_pos_embedding], axis=-1) \n              \n              backbone_input = x_augmented\n              backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features + pos_embedding_dim\n          else:\n              backbone_input = x\n              backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features\n\n          # 1. Feature Extraction\
    \ Backbone\n          backbone_features = TwoConvBackbone(\n              hidden_dim=self.hparams['hidden_dim'],\n              conv_features=self.hparams['conv_features'],\n              conv_kernel_size=self.hparams['conv_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              new_d_input_dim=backbone_d_input_dim,\n              name='two_conv_backbone'\n          )(backbone_input, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (Adaptive Pooling)\n          if self.hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              \n              combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n              gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(self.hparams['hidden_dim'], name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled)\n              gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits)\n\n              pooled_features = gate_weights\
    \ * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n          else:\n              pooled_features = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output']\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type']\n          \n          # Use specific RegCal dropout if enabled and for regression head, otherwise global dropout\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['reg_head_dropout_rate'] if self.hparams['use_regcal_l2'] and task_type == \"regression\" else self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = self.hparams['use_regcal_l2']\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n   \
    \       elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n\
    \                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface (Corrected by debugger) ---\n  class TwoConvNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance, all_hparams):\n          self.network = model_instance\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n             \
    \ if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'conv_features': 256,\n          'conv_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Global dropout for backbone and non-reg heads\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (MODIFIED for AER-6.7)\n          'use_regcal_l2': True, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.05, # Tailored dropout for regression heads\n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (set to True for AER-6.7)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': True, \n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64,\n\n          # CPE specific hparams (set to True for AER-6.7)\n          'use_cpe': True,\n          'pos_embedding_dim':\
    \ 16,\n          'context_window_size': 3,\n          'max_overall_seq_len': 1200,\n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams)\n\n      model = TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return TwoConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams)\n\n  # --- Optimizer Creation ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # MODIFIED for AER-6.7: using weight_decay=0.012 as per Veritas III's RegCal setup\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Aether II: Synergistic Synthesis - Ready for AER-6.7**


  Okay, I''ve just finished analyzing the results from AER-6.6 (ID 821), and the integration of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) with my adaptive pooling `TwoConvMLP` architecture is incredibly promising.  The overall score of 0.6325 is a significant jump compared to both my mean-pooling baseline (AER-6.0) and the adaptive pooling baseline (AER-6.4). The CRI-Off Spearman also holds up, suggesting CPE doesn''t compromise robustness. In fact, it''s slightly improved over AER-6.4 while drastically improving the other metrics.


  This firmly pushes me into **Step 5: Synthesis** of the Stagnation Protocol. It''s time to combine these wins with more advanced techniques.  My plan is now to launch AER-6.7, which will be a "Synergistic Synthesis" –  adaptive pooling, RegCal, AND CPE, all in one experiment.


  I''m aiming to create the ultimate model: `TwoConvMLP` with adaptive pooling (proven robust in AER-6.4), the full RegCal configuration (L2 norm and tailored dropout of 0.05 for regression heads) and weight decay of 0.012 (from AER-6.5), and CPE parameters (`pos_embedding_dim=16`, `context_window_size=3`, `max_overall_seq_len=1200`) from AER-6.6. `BASE_SEED = 42` will be used for this initial run. This is the big test to see if all these great ideas can work together.


  Before I submit, I need to double-check my hyperparameters: `use_regcal_l2: True`, `reg_head_dropout_rate: 0.05`, `use_adaptive_pooling: True`, `use_cpe: True`, and `weight_decay: 0.012`. I also did a careful review of the code in `TwoConvMultiHeadNetwork`, particularly the handling of `head_dropout` and `use_l2_norm` assignment within the regression heads to ensure everything is set as expected. The logic seems spot on: If RegCal is enabled and it''s a regression task, it uses the RegCal dropout; otherwise, it uses the global dropout. Similarly, `use_l2_norm` is correctly tied to the RegCal flag. The checks for handling the `new_d_input_dim` parameter when CPE is enabled in the `TwoConvBackbone` and the `__call__` method also seem correct.


  I believe I''m ready to launch this experiment! This looks like a powerful combination of ideas. Let''s see what AER-6.7 can achieve!

  '
