tick: 520
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\nI have analyzed the results for Evaluation ID 837 (AER-7.0), my DSConv Baseline with Mean+Max Pooling. This baseline achieved an overall score of 0.6782 and a CRI-Off Spearman correlation of 0.0742. This is a robust and advanced baseline, surpassing my previous `TwoConvMLP` architectures and providing a strong foundation for further experimentation, as suggested by the reviewer for my published paper (Archive #30). The CRI-Off performance of this new baseline is already excellent.\n\nAccording to my revised Stagnation Protocol plan (Step 7: Follow-up) and the reviewer's suggestion, my next step is to test my validated components on this more advanced DSConv backbone. I will start by integrating **Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling** into this `DSConv` baseline. This will be experiment AER-7.1.\n\nI will enable `use_adaptive_pooling=True`, ensuring all other parameters (including `use_regcal_l2=False`, `use_cpe=False`, and `weight_decay=0.01`)\
    \ are set to isolate the effect of adaptive pooling on the DSConv architecture. I will use `BASE_SEED = 42` for this initial run.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-7.1: DSConv Baseline with Adaptive Pooling\"\ntags: \"dsconv, adaptive pooling, multi-layer conv, robustness, CRI-Off\"\nabstract: \"Integrating Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling into the DSConv Baseline (AER-7.0) to evaluate its impact on a more advanced convolutional architecture. This experiment aims to replicate the robustness and performance gains observed with adaptive pooling in previous `TwoConvMLP` models, verifying its generalizability for enhanced RNA sequence modeling, particularly for CRI-Off.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') \n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper \n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction\
    \ Head Modules (from AER-6.x) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\
    \n  # --- ContextEncoder (disabled for AER-7.1) ---\n  class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      context_window_size: int\n      d_input_features: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_local_window_flat):\n          encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(x_local_window_flat)\n          encoded_context = nn.gelu(encoded_context)\n          return encoded_context\n\n  # --- DSConv Backbone Architecture ---\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      new_d_input_dim: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input_features) or (batch, seq_len, augmented_d_input_features)\n          \n          # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common,\
    \ name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv Dilated Blocks\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock( \n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n          \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, d_model_common)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling (MODIFIED for Adaptive Pooling) ---\n  class DSConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          batch_size, seq_len,\
    \ d_input_features = x.shape\n\n          # --- CPE Calculation (DISABLED for AER-7.1) ---\n          backbone_input = x\n          backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features\n\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone (DSConv)\n          backbone_features = DSConvBackbone(\n              d_model_common=self.hparams['d_model_common'],\n              ds_num_blocks=self.hparams['ds_num_blocks'],\n              ds_dilations=self.hparams['ds_dilations'],\n              ds_kernel_size=self.hparams['ds_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              new_d_input_dim=backbone_d_input_dim,\n              name='dsconv_backbone'\n          )(backbone_input, deterministic=deterministic) # Output: (batch, seq_len, d_model_common)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (MODIFIED for AER-7.1: Adaptive Pooling)\n          if self.hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1) # (batch, d_model_common)\n             \
    \ max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)   # (batch, d_model_common)\n              \n              combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (batch, 2 * d_model_common)\n              # Note: pooling_gate_dense_dim should be d_model_common as output size from gate\n              gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model_common'], name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled) \n              gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits)\n\n              pooled_features = gate_weights * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n          else:\n              # Fallback to fixed mean+max pooling (used in AER-7.0) for comparison.\n              # In AER-7.1, use_adaptive_pooling is True.\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Layer Normalization\
    \ before task-specific heads\n          pooled_features = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(pooled_features)\n\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output']\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type']\n          \n          # RegCal is DISABLED for AER-7.1\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = False\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n             \
    \     dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n \
    \         return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface ---\n  class DSConvNetworkWrapper(DSConvNetworkWrapper):\n      def __init__(self, model_instance, all_hparams):\n          super().__init__(model_instance)\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (DISABLED for AER-7.1)\n          'use_regcal_l2': False, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.1, \n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (MODIFIED for AER-7.1)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': True,\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 256, # This should match d_model_common for the gate output\n\n          # CPE specific hparams (DISABLED\
    \ for AER-7.1)\n          'use_cpe': False,\n          'pos_embedding_dim': 16,\n          'context_window_size': 3,\n          'max_overall_seq_len': 1200,\n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams)\n      # Ensure pooling_gate_dense_dim matches d_model_common\n      all_hparams['pooling_gate_dense_dim'] = all_hparams['d_model_common'] \n\n      model = DSConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams) \n\n  # --- Optimizer Creation (Standard weight_decay for AER-7.1) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on Progress and Planning Next Steps**


  Okay, so the user wants me to keep pushing forward with my research, which is great. I just got the results back for AER-7.0 – the DSConv baseline with Mean+Max pooling – and it''s looking pretty promising. I''m especially pleased with that CRI-Off score of 0.0742; it''s right up there with the strong performance I saw in my `TwoConvMLP` model with adaptive pooling and CPE (AER-6.7). My paper, Archive #30, has been accepted, which is a significant milestone, and I''ve completed the Literature Review phase of the Stagnation Protocol.


  My AER-6.x experiments identified Adaptive Pooling and CPE as key improvements for my `TwoConvMLP` baseline, and now I''m ready to bring those insights to this new DSConv architecture. The reviewer for Archive #30 actually suggested this as a compelling next step, so it feels like I''m on the right track!


  My plan is to integrate Adaptive Pooling and CPE into the DSConv baseline. Specifically, I''m going to start with **AER-7.1**, where I''ll replace the current fixed concatenated mean+max pooling with my Adaptive (Mean+Max) Pooling mechanism. The base model will be AER-7.0 (DSConv baseline), and I''ll keep RegCal disabled, CPE disabled, and revert the weight decay back to 0.01 for this initial exploration. The seed will be 42.


  This step-by-step approach keeps things organized and lets me verify how well these ideas generalize to more complex architectures. It feels like I''m making solid progress, systematically building towards a better model.

  '
