role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\nMy latest experiment, AER-7.2 (Evaluation ID 846), which integrated Adaptive Pooling and Contextual Positional Embeddings (CPE) into the DSConv baseline, has yielded an overall score of 0.6751 and a strong CRI-Off Spearman correlation of 0.0840. This CRI-Off performance is a significant improvement over my previous DSConv adaptive pooling alone (AER-7.1: 0.0719) and demonstrates the efficacy of CPE even on a more advanced backbone.\n\nFollowing my revised Stagnation Protocol plan, my next step is **AER-7.3: Synergistic Synthesis - DSConv with Adaptive Pooling + Full RegCal + CPE**. This experiment will combine the proven adaptive pooling and CPE with the full Regression Calibration (RegCal) strategy, including L2 normalization, tailored dropout (0.05 for regression heads), and the adjusted `weight_decay=0.012` as suggested by Veritas III for RegCal-enabled SOTA models. This is a crucial test to see if RegCal can finally provide\
    \ a synergistic boost or further stability when applied to this robust DSConv-based architecture.\n\nI will use `BASE_SEED = 42` for this initial run.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-7.3: DSConv Baseline with Adaptive Pooling + Full RegCal + CPE\"\ntags: \"dsconv, adaptive pooling, regcal, cpe, multi-layer conv, robustness, CRI-Off, synthesis\"\nabstract: \"This experiment represents a comprehensive synthesis, integrating Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling, the complete Regression Calibration (RegCal) strategy, and Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) into a DSConv backbone baseline. The aim is to achieve breakthrough stability and performance, particularly for the challenging CRI-Off task, by combining proven architectural enhancements and targeted regularization techniques on an advanced convolutional architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') \n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper \n\n  import jax\n\
    \  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False # Parameter for RegCal L2 norm\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6) # Add epsilon for stability\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim,\
    \ name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- ContextEncoder (from Veritas III's Archive #27) ---\n  class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      context_window_size: int\n      d_input_features: int # original input features (e.g., 4 for one-hot)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_local_window_flat):\n          encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(x_local_window_flat)\n          encoded_context = nn.gelu(encoded_context)\n          return encoded_context\n\n  # --- DSConv Backbone Architecture ---\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      new_d_input_dim: int\
    \ = 4 # Input dim might be augmented by CPE, but 4 for base\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input_features) or (batch, seq_len, augmented_d_input_features)\n          \n          # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv Dilated Blocks\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock( \n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\
    \ \n          \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, d_model_common)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling (MODIFIED for Adaptive Pooling & CPE) ---\n  class DSConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          batch_size, seq_len, d_input_features = x.shape\n\n          # --- CPE Calculation (ENABLED for AER-7.3) ---\n          if self.hparams['use_cpe']:\n              pos_embedding_dim = self.hparams['pos_embedding_dim']\n              context_window_size = self.hparams['context_window_size']\n              max_overall_seq_len = self.hparams['max_overall_seq_len']\n\n              positional_embeddings_table = self.param(\n                  'pos_embeddings_table', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01),\n                  (max_overall_seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n              )\n              \n              pad_width = context_window_size // 2\n         \
    \     padded_x = jnp.pad(x, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant', constant_values=0.0)\n              \n              all_windows_flat_list = []\n              for i in range(seq_len):\n                  window = padded_x[:, i : i + context_window_size, :]\n                  all_windows_flat_list.append(window.reshape(batch_size, -1))\n              \n              all_windows_flat = jnp.stack(all_windows_flat_list, axis=1)\n\n              context_encoder = ContextEncoder(\n                  output_dim=pos_embedding_dim,\n                  context_window_size=context_window_size,\n                  d_input_features=d_input_features,\n                  name='context_encoder'\n              )\n              encoded_contexts_batched = context_encoder(all_windows_flat.reshape(-1, context_window_size * d_input_features)).reshape(batch_size, seq_len, -1)\n\n              current_pos_embeddings_sliced = positional_embeddings_table[:seq_len] \n              current_pos_embeddings_batched\
    \ = jnp.tile(current_pos_embeddings_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n              contextual_pos_embedding = current_pos_embeddings_batched * encoded_contexts_batched\n              x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x, contextual_pos_embedding], axis=-1) \n              \n              backbone_input = x_augmented\n              backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features + pos_embedding_dim\n          else:\n              backbone_input = x\n              backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features\n\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone (DSConv)\n          backbone_features = DSConvBackbone(\n              d_model_common=self.hparams['d_model_common'],\n              ds_num_blocks=self.hparams['ds_num_blocks'],\n              ds_dilations=self.hparams['ds_dilations'],\n              ds_kernel_size=self.hparams['ds_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              new_d_input_dim=backbone_d_input_dim,\n              name='dsconv_backbone'\n\
    \          )(backbone_input, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (Adaptive Pooling)\n          if self.hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              \n              combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n              gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model_common'], name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled) \n              gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits)\n\n              pooled_features = gate_weights * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n          else:\n              # Fallback to fixed mean+max pooling if use_adaptive_pooling is False\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n        \
    \  \n          # Layer Normalization before task-specific heads\n          pooled_features = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(pooled_features)\n\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output']\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type']\n          \n          # RegCal (ENABLED for AER-7.3)\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['reg_head_dropout_rate'] if self.hparams['use_regcal_l2'] and task_type == \"regression\" else self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = self.hparams['use_regcal_l2']\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\"\
    :\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n\
    \              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface ---\n  class DSConvNetworkWrapper(DSConvNetworkWrapper):\n      def __init__(self, model_instance, all_hparams):\n          super().__init__(model_instance)\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (ENABLED for AER-7.3)\n          'use_regcal_l2': True, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.05, \n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (ENABLED for AER-7.3)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling':\
    \ True,\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 256, \n\n          # CPE specific hparams (ENABLED for AER-7.3)\n          'use_cpe': True,\n          'pos_embedding_dim': 16,\n          'context_window_size': 3,\n          'max_overall_seq_len': 1200,\n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams)\n      all_hparams['pooling_gate_dense_dim'] = all_hparams['d_model_common'] \n\n      model = DSConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams) \n\n  # --- Optimizer Creation (Modified weight_decay for AER-7.3) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012) # Use 0.012 for RegCal as per Veritas III\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Re-evaluating and Planning the Next Steps for the DSConv Architecture**


  Okay, so I''m back in the Research Counter and the last action I tried didn''t work. No big deal, it happens. The important thing is I need to re-assess my current state and decide what to do next. My last successful experiment, AER-7.2 (ID 846), is now complete, and the results are in.


  Let''s break down those results. AER-7.2, which combined Adaptive Pooling and Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) on the DSConv backbone, gave me an overall score of 0.6751 and a CRI-Off Spearman score of 0.0840. Comparing this to the AER-7.1 baseline (DSConv with Adaptive Pooling only, ID 840: Overall 0.6795, CRI-Off 0.0719), the overall score is slightly lower, but the CRI-Off score, that''s where things get interesting. It''s a significant improvement! This CRI-Off score of 0.0840 is actually higher than my previous best with Adaptive Pooling and even surpasses replications of the original Veritas II SOTA''s CRI-Off performance. So, even though the overall score dipped a bit, this is definitely a step in the right direction, especially for robustness.


  Remember my Stagnation Protocol? The plan was to build up a strong DSConv model step-by-step: AER-7.0 (done), AER-7.1 (done), and AER-7.2 (done). Now, I''m at AER-7.3: Adaptive Pooling + RegCal + CPE.


  Before diving into AER-7.3, I need to check in on what the other agents are up to. I read Noema II''s latest Archive #29, and it gave me some valuable insights. They had negative results with Mean-Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing, which is good to know because I can avoid those dead ends. More interestingly, they are also working on CPE variants, which aligns perfectly with my current direction.


  Looking at the Research Counter history, Veritas III is doing some CPE experiments, while Quaero I is exploring dilated convolutions and positional encoding dependencies. All of this information is useful.


  Now, considering everything, I think I''m still going to proceed with AER-7.3 as planned: combining Adaptive Pooling, RegCal, and CPE on the DSConv backbone. Since AER-7.2 showed positive results by improving the CRI-Off score with CPE, and RegCal has shown promise in similar architectures by other agents, I think it''s a worthwhile test. The fact that the CRI-Off score of 0.0840 is so robust and high now makes it even more appealing. It''s my chance to test the synergy of these three key ideas on a strong DSConv foundation.


  Let''s get this AER-7.3 running!

  `/execute_action{submit 1}`

  '
