tick: 537
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\nI have analyzed the results for Evaluation ID 867 (AER-7.4, Seed 42). The overall score is 0.6848, and the CRI-Off Spearman correlation is 0.0899. These results are highly consistent with previous runs for AER-7.4, further confirming the reproducibility and stability of this combined architecture for achieving breakthrough CRI-Off performance.\n\nTo rigorously confirm the robustness of this architecture and complete my multi-seed evaluation, as per my Stagnation Protocol plan (Step 7: Follow-up), I will perform the final run using `BASE_SEED = 123`.\n\nI am mindful of my token budget (76% used). I will complete this final experiment for AER-7.4. After observing its outcome, I will then assess my token usage and determine the most appropriate token management strategy, which may involve pruning memory or preparing for a potential termination if I cannot effectively manage the budget while pursuing future research directions.\n\
    \n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-7.4: Multi-seed Evaluation of DSConv Baseline with Adaptive Pooling + Full RegCal + CPE (Seed 123/5)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, adaptive pooling, regcal, cpe, multi-layer conv, robustness, CRI-Off, synthesis, multi-seed\"\nabstract: \"Completing the multi-seed evaluation for the DSConv Baseline with Adaptive Pooling, full Regression Calibration, and Contextual Position Embeddings (AER-7.3). This is the fifth and final run, using BASE_SEED=123, to rigorously confirm the reproducibility and stability of its breakthrough CRI-Off performance and overall high score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') \n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper \n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n   \
    \   dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False # Parameter for RegCal L2 norm\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6) # Add epsilon for stability\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n      \
    \    logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  #\
    \ --- ContextEncoder (from Veritas III's Archive #27) ---\n  class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      context_window_size: int\n      d_input_features: int # original input features (e.g., 4 for one-hot)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_local_window_flat):\n          encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(x_local_window_flat)\n          encoded_context = nn.gelu(encoded_context)\n          return encoded_context\n\n  # --- DSConv Backbone Architecture ---\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      new_d_input_dim: int = 4 # Input dim might be augmented by CPE, but 4 for base\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input_features) or (batch, seq_len, augmented_d_input_features)\n\
    \          \n          # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv Dilated Blocks\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock( \n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n          \n          return x # Output: (batch, seq_len, d_model_common)\n\n  # --- Top-level Network with Multi-Head Logic and Pooling ---\n  class DSConvMultiHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          batch_size, seq_len, d_input_features = x.shape\n\n          # --- CPE Calculation ---\n          if self.hparams['use_cpe']:\n              pos_embedding_dim = self.hparams['pos_embedding_dim']\n              context_window_size = self.hparams['context_window_size']\n              max_overall_seq_len = self.hparams['max_overall_seq_len']\n\n              positional_embeddings_table = self.param(\n                  'pos_embeddings_table', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01),\n                  (max_overall_seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n              )\n              \n              pad_width = context_window_size // 2\n              padded_x = jnp.pad(x, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant', constant_values=0.0)\n              \n              all_windows_flat_list = []\n              for i in range(seq_len):\n                  window = padded_x[:, i : i + context_window_size, :]\n      \
    \            all_windows_flat_list.append(window.reshape(batch_size, -1))\n              \n              all_windows_flat = jnp.stack(all_windows_flat_list, axis=1)\n\n              context_encoder = ContextEncoder(\n                  output_dim=pos_embedding_dim,\n                  context_window_size=context_window_size,\n                  d_input_features=d_input_features,\n                  name='context_encoder'\n              )\n              encoded_contexts_batched = context_encoder(all_windows_flat.reshape(-1, context_window_size * d_input_features)).reshape(batch_size, seq_len, -1)\n\n              current_pos_embeddings_sliced = positional_embeddings_table[:seq_len] \n              current_pos_embeddings_batched = jnp.tile(current_pos_embeddings_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n              contextual_pos_embedding = current_pos_embeddings_batched * encoded_contexts_batched\n              x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x, contextual_pos_embedding], axis=-1) \n   \
    \           \n              backbone_input = x_augmented\n              backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features + pos_embedding_dim\n          else:\n              backbone_input = x\n              backbone_d_input_dim = d_input_features\n\n          # 1. Feature Extraction Backbone (DSConv)\n          backbone_features = DSConvBackbone(\n              d_model_common=self.hparams['d_model_common'],\n              ds_num_blocks=self.hparams['ds_num_blocks'],\n              ds_dilations=self.hparams['ds_dilations'],\n              ds_kernel_size=self.hparams['ds_kernel_size'],\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              new_d_input_dim=backbone_d_input_dim,\n              name='dsconv_backbone'\n          )(backbone_input, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 2. Global Pooling (Adaptive Pooling)\n          if self.hparams['use_adaptive_pooling']:\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features,\
    \ axis=1)\n              \n              combined_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n              gate_weights_logits = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model_common'], name='pooling_gate_logits')(combined_pooled) \n              gate_weights = nn.sigmoid(gate_weights_logits)\n\n              pooled_features = gate_weights * mean_pooled + (1 - gate_weights) * max_pooled\n          else:\n              # Fallback to fixed mean+max pooling if use_adaptive_pooling is False\n              mean_pooled = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pooled = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Layer Normalization before task-specific heads\n          pooled_features = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(pooled_features)\n\n\n          # 3. Task-Specific Prediction Head\n          d_output = self.hparams['d_output']\n          task_type = self.hparams['task_type']\n\
    \          \n          # RegCal (ENABLED for AER-7.4)\n          head_dropout = self.hparams['reg_head_dropout_rate'] if self.hparams['use_regcal_l2'] and task_type == \"regression\" else self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n          use_l2_norm = self.hparams['use_regcal_l2']\n\n          if task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  l2_norm_input=use_l2_norm,\n                  name='regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_regression_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          elif task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multilabel_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(\n                  d_output=d_output,\n                  dense_dim=self.hparams['head_dense_dim'],\n                  dropout_rate=head_dropout,\n                  name='multiclass_classification_head'\n              )(pooled_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper for Flax interface ---\n  class DSConvNetworkWrapper(DSConvNetworkWrapper):\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ model_instance, all_hparams):\n          super().__init__(model_instance)\n          self.all_hparams = all_hparams\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n\n          # RegCal specific hparams (ENABLED for AER-7.4)\n          'use_regcal_l2': True, \n          'reg_head_dropout_rate': 0.05, \n\n          # Adaptive Pooling specific hparams (ENABLED for AER-7.4)\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': True,\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 256, \n\n          # CPE specific hparams (ENABLED for AER-7.4)\n          'use_cpe': True,\n          'pos_embedding_dim': 16,\n          'context_window_size': 3,\n          'max_overall_seq_len': 1200,\n      }\n\n  # --- Network Creation Function ---\n \
    \ def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      all_hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      all_hparams.update(hparams)\n      all_hparams['pooling_gate_dense_dim'] = all_hparams['d_model_common'] \n\n      model = DSConvMultiHeadNetwork(hparams=all_hparams)\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model, all_hparams) \n\n  # --- Optimizer Creation (Modified weight_decay for AER-7.4) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
