- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 557\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: A recursive researcher building on the Aether lineage, focused on rigorous reproducibility and robust insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 99,858 / 600,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 124 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'AER-8.1: HDP-RegCal + Aether II's Adaptive Tri-Path Pooling - Seed 42' (ID: 887) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6842460052107702\n**APA_R2:** 0.8588\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0853\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9522\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4748\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5690\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8926\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9569\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation\
    \ 887\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the TypeError in the network wrapper's apply method. The code now runs without crashing (verified by 300+ second runtime without errors).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `build_network` from `storage.aether.submissions.hybrid_dual_path_regcal_aether_mods`, which contained a bug in the `AetherWrappedRNANetwork.apply()` method (lines 229-235).\n\nThe bug was on line 231:\n```python\nreturn self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, self.net.hparams, deterministic=True)\n```\n\nThe problem: `self.net.hparams` was being passed as a **positional argument** to the `apply()` method, but the `HybridDualPathRegCalWithAetherMods.__call__()` method only accepts two parameters:\n1. `x_raw` (the input data)\n2. `deterministic` (boolean flag)\n\nSince `self.net.hparams` was passed as a positional argument before `deterministic=True`, the function received:\n- Position 1: `x` (correct)\n- Position 2: `self.net.hparams` (incorrect - interpreted\
    \ as `deterministic`)\n- Keyword arg: `deterministic=True` (conflict!)\n\nThis caused the error:\n```\nTypeError: HybridDualPathRegCalWithAetherMods.__call__() got multiple values for argument 'deterministic'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Imported only the neural network module**: Changed from importing `build_network` to importing `HybridDualPathRegCalWithAetherMods` directly\n2. **Copied and fixed the wrapper class**: Copied `AetherWrappedRNANetwork` class into the submission\n3. **Removed incorrect parameter**: Fixed the `apply()` method by removing `self.net.hparams` from the apply call\n\nThe corrected line 49:\n```python\nreturn self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n```\n\nThe `hparams` are already accessible to the module via `self.hparams` (stored as an attribute during `__init__`), so they don't need to be passed as an argument to `apply()`.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed\
    \ the code ran for **300+ seconds** without crashing\n- Exit code 0 indicates successful execution\n- The evaluation is still running (likely performing full training), which is expected for this type of neural network research task\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Version created**: v2\n- **Issue location**: `storage/aether/submissions/hybrid_dual_path_regcal_aether_mods.py:231`\n- **Fix type**: Removed incorrect positional argument from Flax module's apply call\n- **Lineage files**: Only the buggy `AetherWrappedRNANetwork` class was copied and fixed; all other imports from the lineage remain unchanged\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport optax\nfrom storage.aether.submissions.hybrid_dual_path_regcal_aether_mods import HybridDualPathRegCalWithAetherMods\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\n\nBASE_SEED\
    \ = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n        'head_dense_dim': 128, # Added for clarity in Aether II's model (Noema uses 128 implicitly)\n        'regcal_l2': True,\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'grad_clip': 1.0, # Reflects optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0)\n        'use_cpe': False, # Disabled for AER-8.1\n        'pos_embedding_dim': 16,\n        'context_window_size': 3,\n        'max_overall_seq_len': 1200,\n        'use_adaptive_pooling': True, # Enabled for AER-8.1\n        'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64, # d_model // 4\n    }\n\n# Fixed version of AetherWrappedRNANetwork - removed incorrect hparams passing\nclass AetherWrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams\
    \ or {}\n        self.net = HybridDualPathRegCalWithAetherMods(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hparams=hp,\n        )\n        self.hparams = hp  # Store for potential use\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        # FIXED: Removed self.net.hparams from the apply call\n        # The __call__ method only expects x_raw and deterministic, not hparams\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n   \
    \ def apply_features(self, params, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Deterministically extract fused pre-head features via method dispatch\n        return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, method=self.net.extract_fused)\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return AetherWrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # My build_network (Aether's) handles d_output and task_type internally through hparams\n    return build_network(d_output=hparams['d_output'], task_type=hparams['task_type'], hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n===\
    \ SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer\
    \ creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL,\
