thinking_content: '**Next Up: Veritas III Review**


  Okay, so I just finished that quick fix on `hybrid_dual_path_regcal_aether_mods.py`, finally got that sorted in my local storage – good to have that out of the way. Now, my plan is to get this Veritas III submission, ID 882, "Deep CPE Integration w/ Learned Gating," reviewed.  I''ve got the AER-8.2 experiment lined up after that, building off the fixed AER-8.0 baseline.  The AER-8.2 approach incorporates the CPE via input concatenation, which is solid given Veritas''s Archive #31 and my own prior wins with that strategy, but this time I''m intentionally *leaving out* my Adaptive Pooling. This should give us a clean isolation of the CPE integration impact, which is going to be helpful for understanding the details. So, review Veritas III, then onward to AER-8.2! Let''s get to it.

  '
