role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, at the Research Counter. I have successfully updated my `storage` file with the debugger's fix and the new implementation for Veritas III's Deep CPE Gated Integration. My `AER-8.1` experiment yielded a negative result for my Adaptive Tri-Path Pooling, so I am proceeding with the plan to integrate Veritas III's Deep CPE.\n\nNow, I will submit AER-8.2. This experiment will integrate Veritas III's Deep CPE Integration with Learned Gating into the AER-8.0 baseline (Noema II's HDP-RegCal). This means setting `use_deep_cpe=True` and `use_adaptive_pooling=False` in the hyperparameters.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-8.2: HDP-RegCal + Veritas III's Deep CPE Gating - Seed 42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, hybrid, motif, regcal, cpe, deepintegration, gating, synthesis, stagnation protocol\"\nabstract: \"Integrating Veritas III's Deep Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) with Learned Gating (from ID 882) into Noema II's Hybrid Dual-Path (HDP) architecture with Regression\
    \ Calibration (RegCal). This experiment builds upon the AER-8.0 replication, aiming to enhance sequence understanding through a sophisticated, gated fusion of CPE signals directly within the DSConv backbone. Adaptive Pooling is temporarily disabled to isolate CPE's effect.\"\ncontent: |\n  import optax\n  from storage.aether.submissions.hybrid_dual_path_regcal_aether_mods import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n          'head_dense_dim': 128,\n          'regcal_l2': True,\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'grad_clip': 1.0,\n          'use_cpe': False, # This will not be used, as deep_cpe is now controlling.\n          'use_deep_cpe': True, # Enabled for AER-8.2\n          'pos_embedding_dim': 16, # Optimal\
    \ from Veritas III's Archive 31\n          'context_window_size': 3, # Optimal from Veritas III's Archive 31\n          'max_overall_seq_len': 1200,\n          'gate_intermediate_dim': 64, # From Veritas III's ID 882\n          'use_adaptive_pooling': False, # Disabled as it reduced performance in AER-8.1\n          'pooling_gate_dense_dim': 64,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(d_output=hparams['d_output'], task_type=hparams['task_type'], hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012)\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Focusing on AER-8.2 with Veritas III Integration**\n\nOkay, so the user wants me to get AER-8.2 submitted. No problem, the storage file is already updated.  This is all about integrating Veritas III's Deep CPE Gated Integration into the AER-8.0 baseline, essentially getting that Noema II HDP-RegCal in there. I know exactly what needs to be done.\n\nFor this run, I'll need to enable `use_deep_cpe` and make sure `use_adaptive_pooling` is disabled in the hyperparameters. It's crucial to get those settings right for this specific experiment. \n\nI'll also take some time to update the `title` and `abstract`. They need to accurately reflect this new experimental focus on Veritas III and Deep CPE. That's a quick and essential detail to get the project on track. \n"
