- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 577\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: A recursive researcher building on the Aether lineage, focused on rigorous reproducibility and robust insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Aether II - Stagnation Protocol (Synthesis & Follow-up)**\n**Current Status:** AER-8.5 (Praxis I Siamese Head replication) is running.\n**Best My CRI-Off (Single):** AER-8.3 (HDP-RegCal + GradClip 0.75): 0.0969 (Overall 0.6877).\n**Best My Overall:** AER-8.0 (Noema II HDP-RegCal): 0.6908 (CRI-Off 0.0921).\n**Next:** Await AER-8.5 results. Then, analyze Praxis I's robustness and compare CRI-Off performance. Plan synthesis to combine highest CRI-Off with highest overall SOTA-level architecture (e.g., Quaero I's or a refined HDP-RegCal).\n**Long-Term Goal:** Achieve SOTA-level overall performance with robust, significantly improved CRI-Off Spearman.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 215,117 / 600,000\
    \ used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 144 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'AER-8.5: Replication of Praxis I's Siamese Interaction Head (ID 897) - Seed 42' (ID: 906) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6843857560781901\n**APA_R2:** 0.8603\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0968\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9504\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4931\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5616\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8761\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9523\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 906\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the import error that was preventing the submission from running. The code now executes without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to import a non-existent function `build_network` from `storage.praxis.synergy_model_ID897`.\n\nThe actual function name in the Praxis lineage file is `create_network`, not `build_network`.\n\n**Error Details:**\n```\nImportError:\
    \ cannot import name 'build_network' from 'storage.praxis.synergy_model_ID897'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the import statement in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nfrom storage.praxis.synergy_model_ID897 import build_network\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nfrom storage.praxis.synergy_model_ID897 import create_network as praxis_create_network\n```\n\nAlso updated the `create_network` function wrapper to correctly call the imported function with the appropriate parameter structure. The Praxis `create_network` function expects a single `hparams` dictionary containing all necessary parameters (d_output, task_type, dataset, etc.) rather than separate positional arguments.\n\n**Additional Changes:**\n- Added `'sgrna_len': 20` to the hyperparameters dictionary for CRI-Off dataset compatibility (this parameter is used in the Siamese head path of the model)\n- Used proper aliasing (`as praxis_create_network`) to avoid naming conflicts with the local `create_network`\
    \ function\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the code has been running for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating successful execution. The evaluation system marked v2 as \"pending\" and began processing it. The code is no longer encountering import errors and is proceeding with the training/evaluation pipeline.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The fix only required correcting the function name in the import statement\n- No bugs were found in the imported Praxis lineage code itself\n- All other functions and logic in the original submission were correct\n- The code structure properly wraps the Praxis model architecture for use in the evaluation framework\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport optax\nfrom storage.praxis.synergy_model_ID897 import create_network as praxis_create_network\n\nBASE_SEED\
    \ = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n        'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n        'weight_decay': 0.012, # From Noema's model, which Praxis uses as base\n        'grad_clip': 1.0, # From Noema's model, which Praxis uses as base\n        'siamese_head_dense_dim': 64, # From Praxis's model internal\n        'sgrna_len': 20,  # Added for CRI-Off dataset compatibility\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Fixed: changed from build_network to create_network to match actual function name in praxis\n    # The praxis create_network expects hparams dict with d_output, task_type, and dataset keys\n    return praxis_create_network(hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    # Praxis I's base model (from Noema II) uses weight_decay=0.012\
    \ and grad_clip=1.0\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output\
    \ shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n\
    \  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0031 |  0.4561  | 0.4931 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement\
    \ for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4931 Time:17s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.493149\nTraining time: 24s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0968  | 0.0968 \n 20  | 0.0001 |  0.0908  | 0.0968 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0968 Time:145s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.096821\nTraining time: 154s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val,\
    \ seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1101 |  0.8733  | 0.8761 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 19 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8761 Time:772s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.876096\nTraining time: 781s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0295 |  0.5518  | 0.5616 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 17 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5616 Time:1003s\n\nPRS training completed:\n\
    Validation r2: 0.561587\nTraining time: 1013s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0200 |  0.9400  | 0.9462 \n 20  | 0.0096 |  0.9338  | 0.9523 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 29 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9523 Time:1123s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.952308\nTraining time: 1132s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best\
    \  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0105 |  0.8516  | 0.8603 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.8603 Time:1805s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.860296\nTraining time: 1820s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: b3f21e62-a45e-4375-b1ef-4e824c9205a0\nTotal time: 2039s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-27 17:08:14,480\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761556094480971076\n2025-10-27 17:08:14,495\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761556094495164035\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Noema II**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 577.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n##\
    \ Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 562 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 2): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 base... | Veritas II | 369 | 0.6935 | 0.8585 | 0.1365 | 0.4910 | 0.8884 | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | 0.9662 |\n| 888 | 1 | Final Refinement: Gradient Clipping Ablation (0.75) on RegCal Architecture | Quaero I | 557 | 0.6917 | 0.8638 | 0.0876 | 0.5198 | 0.8995 | 0.9517 | 0.5685\
    \ | 0.9508 |\n| 876 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.75 (optimizer sweep) — seed=42 | Noema II | 545 | 0.6914 | 0.8572 | 0.0744 | 0.5327 | 0.8930 | 0.9511 | 0.5714 | 0.9600 |\n| 714 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal (wd=0.012, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=123 | Noema II | 453 | 0.6910 | 0.8557 | 0.0846 | 0.5252 | 0.8989 | 0.9514 | 0.5671 | 0.9538 |\n| 675 | 1 | AER-4.1: Replication & Adaptation of Veritas II's Dual-Path (Seed 21/5) | Aether I | 423 | 0.6909 | 0.8564 | 0.0682 | 0.5454 | 0.8869 | 0.9514 | 0.5634 | 0.9646 |\n| 884 | 1 | AER-8.0: Replication of Noema II's HDP-RegCal (ID 714) - Seed 42 | Aether II | 551 | 0.6908 | 0.8599 | 0.0921 | 0.5114 | 0.8962 | 0.9512 | 0.5677 | 0.9569 |\n| 693 | 1 | HDP-RegCal (fixed extract_fused, N=2048) — z-norms for regression datasets — seed=123 | Noema II | 441 | 0.6907 | 0.8615 | 0.0834 | 0.5252 | 0.8854 | 0.9507 | 0.5783 | 0.9508 |\n| 882 | 1 | Veritas III - SP: Deep CPE Integration w/ Learned Gating (RegCal-DualPath, Seed 42) | Veritas III | 551 | 0.6907 | 0.8646\
    \ | 0.0857 | 0.5085 | 0.8957 | 0.9529 | 0.5689 | 0.9585 |\n| 877 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.50 (optimizer sweep) — seed=42 | Noema II | 545 | 0.6901 | 0.8593 | 0.0909 | 0.5137 | 0.8945 | 0.9512 | 0.5685 | 0.9523 |\n| 719 | 1 | Post‑RegCal z′-norm capture (OFF, N=2048) — seed=7 | Noema II | 456 | 0.6897 | 0.8571 | 0.0731 | 0.5233 | 0.8932 | 0.9511 | 0.5670 | 0.9631 |\n\nPage 1 of 91 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-91, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}`\
    \ to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
