thinking_content: '**Praxis I Replication & Protocol Update**


  Okay, so I just finished submitting AER-8.7, which completes the multi-seed replication for Praxis I''s Siamese Head. It came in with a decent score, 0.6868 overall and a CRI-Off of 0.0960. Now that all three seeds are done, it''s time to analyze the results and adjust the meta prompt.


  Here''s the breakdown of the Praxis I multi-seed runs: AER-8.5, AER-8.6, and AER-8.7.


  *   **ID 906 (Seed 42):** Overall 0.6844, CRI-Off 0.0968

  *   **ID 912 (Seed 7):** Overall 0.6834, CRI-Off 0.0976

  *   **ID 915 (Seed 123):** Overall 0.6868, CRI-Off 0.0960


  Calculating the stats, we have very stable performance.  The overall scores average around 0.6849 with a tiny standard deviation, and the CRI-Offs average around 0.0968.  This confirms strong stability and high CRI-Off performance.


  **My "Best My" scores are now:**


  *   **Best CRI-Off (Median/Robust):** Praxis I''s Siamese Head (AER-8.5-8.7 median) at 0.0968 (with an overall score of ~0.6844). This is now my reliably validated best CRI-Off!

  *   **Best CRI-Off (Single):** Still AER-8.3 at 0.0969 (with an overall of 0.6877). However, Praxis I is much more robust.

  *   **Best Overall (Single):** Quaero I (ID 909) at 0.6942 (CRI-Off 0.0892) - this is the current station SOTA.

  *   **Best Overall (Robust):** AER-8.0 at 0.6908 (CRI-Off 0.0921) - my own robust baseline.


  The Stagnation Protocol (Synthesis & Follow-up) calls for these steps: First, I need to update my internal knowledge base (Private Memory #4) with the full multi-seed results for Praxis I, including those median and standard deviation calculations. This will also require updating the "best CRI-Off options" based on the new robust validation. Secondly, I need to update the meta prompt to reflect Praxis I''s now robust CRI-Off score and the new best overall from Quaero I. Finally, I''ll review Quaero I''s Evaluation ID 909 using `review 909` to understand how they achieved SOTA. After that, I can plan how best to combine the strong CRI-Off strategies from Praxis I with the overall excellence of Quaero I.

  '
