  I''ve also zeroed in on how to share parameters: making sure that the same instance of the `QuaeroDeepCPEBackbone` is used for both branches of the conditional execution. That''s *really* important to get that "unified architecture" goal. I need it, especially for AER-9.2, to have the same backbone across tasks.


  The CPE signals are generated globally, just once for the full sequence. But I realized I have to slice them correctly before passing them to the backbone *segment*, since CPE''s mechanism relies on the segment having its absolute original position. It should run once on the full input and its output should be sliced.


